1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,960
If you're overwhelmed tonight, you're in a
good place to be.

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:08,340
Nothing here asks anything of you.

3
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:15,580
In a moment I'll begin reading the Gospel
of John from the beginning, slowly, all the

4
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:16,520
way through.

5
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:19,300
Let it be the last voice you hear.

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,420
Get comfortable and close your eyes.

7
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:28,120
If something has you overwhelmed tonight, leave
it in the comments — you'll be prayed

8
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,820
for here, and you won't be the only one.

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,480
Subscribe if you'd like this to be part of
your nights.

10
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:39,960
Jesus, I'm overwhelmed tonight, and I
can't argue myself out of it.

11
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:42,120
It isn't one large thing.

12
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:48,820
It's a dozen small ones standing close together,
and from where I'm lying they look like

13
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:49,760
a wall.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,080
I know what I'd say to someone else in
this bed.

15
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,340
I'd tell them most of what they fear won't
happen, and that the part that does happen

16
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:02,280
won't come alone — you'll be in it with
them.

17
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:06,640
I believe that for other people more
easily than I believe it for myself.

18
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:10,740
So let me hear it in your own words
instead of mine.

19
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:17,940
Let John's account of you be the voice in
the room tonight: the way you spoke to people

20
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:23,040
who were frightened, the way you never
once told them they were foolish for it.

21
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,620
You didn't scold the disciples in the
storm.

22
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:27,760
You stood up in the boat.

23
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:29,900
Stand up in this one.

24
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:36,860
Not necessarily to change anything by morning —
just to be here, so that I stop bracing.

25
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:38,860
Loosen my jaw.

26
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:40,380
Slow my chest.

27
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:42,340
Take the watch from me.

28
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:48,400
And be near to everyone listening tonight
who is more afraid than they let on.

29
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:50,160
Amen.

30
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:53,260
John, chapter one.

31
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:58,840
In the beginning was the Word, and the
Word was with God, and the Word was God.

32
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,940
The same was in the beginning with God.

33
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,220
All things were made through him.

34
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,900
Without him, nothing was made that has
been made.

35
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:12,280
In him was life, and the life was the
light of men.

36
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:17,780
The light shines in the darkness, and the
darkness hasn’t overcome it.

37
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:22,440
There came a man sent from God, whose name
was John.

38
00:02:22,958 --> 00:02:29,318
The same came as a witness, that he
might testify about the light, that all might believe

39
00:02:29,358 --> 00:02:30,258
through him.

40
00:02:30,898 --> 00:02:35,578
He was not the light, but was sent that he
might testify about the light.

41
00:02:36,618 --> 00:02:40,518
The true light that enlightens everyone
was coming into the world.

42
00:02:41,318 --> 00:02:46,638
He was in the world, and the world
was made through him, and the world didn’t recognise

43
00:02:46,678 --> 00:02:47,578
him.

44
00:02:48,018 --> 00:02:52,458
He came to his own, and those who were his
own didn’t receive him.

45
00:02:52,958 --> 00:02:59,078
But as many as received him, to them he
gave the right to become God’s children, to those

46
00:02:59,118 --> 00:03:05,858
who believe in his name: who were born, not
of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor

47
00:03:05,898 --> 00:03:07,918
of the will of man, but of God.

48
00:03:08,838 --> 00:03:12,218
The Word became flesh and lived amongst
us.

49
00:03:12,778 --> 00:03:19,298
We saw his glory, such glory as of the
only born Son of the Father, full

50
00:03:19,338 --> 00:03:20,558
of grace and truth.

51
00:03:21,198 --> 00:03:23,418
John testified about him.

52
00:03:24,198 --> 00:03:30,798
He cried out, saying, “This was he of whom
I said, ‘He who comes after me has surpassed

53
00:03:30,838 --> 00:03:37,558
me, for he was before me.’” From his
fullness we all received grace upon

54
00:03:37,598 --> 00:03:38,498
grace.

55
00:03:38,618 --> 00:03:40,678
For the law was given through Moses.

56
00:03:41,558 --> 00:03:44,738
Grace and truth were realised through
Jesus Christ.

57
00:03:45,798 --> 00:03:48,078
No one has seen God at any time.

58
00:03:48,818 --> 00:03:53,818
The only born Son, who is in the bosom of
the Father, has declared him.

59
00:03:54,398 --> 00:04:00,818
This is John’s testimony, when the Jews
sent priests and Levites from Jerusalem to ask

60
00:04:00,858 --> 00:04:02,378
him, “Who are you?”

61
00:04:03,238 --> 00:04:08,598
He declared, and didn’t deny, but he
declared, “I am not the Christ.”

62
00:04:09,578 --> 00:04:11,378
They asked him, “What then?

63
00:04:12,098 --> 00:04:12,998
Are you Elijah?”

64
00:04:13,558 --> 00:04:15,138
He said, “I am not.”

65
00:04:15,698 --> 00:04:16,818
“Are you the prophet?”

66
00:04:17,538 --> 00:04:18,778
He answered, “No.”

67
00:04:19,718 --> 00:04:22,378
They said therefore to him, “Who are you?

68
00:04:22,998 --> 00:04:26,018
Give us an answer to take back to those
who sent us.

69
00:04:26,778 --> 00:04:28,178
What do you say about yourself?”

70
00:04:29,378 --> 00:04:35,218
He said, “I am the voice of one crying
in the wilderness, ‘Make straight the way of the

71
00:04:35,258 --> 00:04:37,698
Lord,’ as Isaiah the prophet said.”

72
00:04:37,738 --> 00:04:41,418
The ones who had been sent were from the
Pharisees.

73
00:04:42,138 --> 00:04:49,338
They asked him, “Why then do you baptise
if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor

74
00:04:49,378 --> 00:04:50,266
the prophet?”

75
00:04:50,306 --> 00:04:56,871
John answered them, “I baptise in water,
but amongst you stands one whom you don’t

76
00:04:56,911 --> 00:04:57,330
know.

77
00:04:57,370 --> 00:05:04,211
He is the one who comes after me, who is
preferred before me, whose sandal

78
00:05:04,251 --> 00:05:06,963
strap I’m not worthy to loosen.”

79
00:05:07,003 --> 00:05:12,926
These things were done in Bethany beyond
the Jordan, where John was baptising.

80
00:05:12,966 --> 00:05:19,807
The next day, he saw Jesus coming to him,
and said, “Behold, the Lamb of

81
00:05:19,847 --> 00:05:22,126
God, who takes away the sin of the world!

82
00:05:23,246 --> 00:05:30,006
This is he of whom I said, ‘After me comes
a man who is preferred before me, for

83
00:05:30,046 --> 00:05:31,146
he was before me.’

84
00:05:31,726 --> 00:05:37,946
I didn’t know him, but for this reason I
came baptising in water, that he would be revealed

85
00:05:37,986 --> 00:05:38,886
to Israel.”

86
00:05:40,086 --> 00:05:46,166
John testified, saying, “I have seen the
Spirit descending like a dove out of heaven,

87
00:05:46,806 --> 00:05:48,126
and it remained on him.

88
00:05:48,546 --> 00:05:55,386
I didn’t recognise him, but he who sent me
to baptise in water said to me, ‘On

89
00:05:55,426 --> 00:06:01,606
whomever you will see the Spirit descending and
remaining on him is he who baptises in

90
00:06:01,646 --> 00:06:02,546
the Holy Spirit.’

91
00:06:03,346 --> 00:06:07,666
I have seen and have testified that this
is the Son of God.”

92
00:06:08,426 --> 00:06:14,926
Again, the next day, John was standing with
two of his disciples, and he looked at

93
00:06:14,966 --> 00:06:20,226
Jesus as he walked, and said, “Behold, the
Lamb of God!”

94
00:06:21,466 --> 00:06:25,066
The two disciples heard him speak, and
they followed Jesus.

95
00:06:25,726 --> 00:06:31,366
Jesus turned and saw them following, and
said to them, “What are you looking for?”

96
00:06:32,046 --> 00:06:39,286
They said to him, “Rabbi” (which is to
say, being interpreted, Teacher), “where

97
00:06:39,326 --> 00:06:40,226
are you staying?”

98
00:06:41,286 --> 00:06:43,246
He said to them, “Come and see.”

99
00:06:43,686 --> 00:06:48,066
They came and saw where he was staying,
and they stayed with him that day.

100
00:06:49,206 --> 00:06:50,646
It was about the tenth hour.

101
00:06:51,626 --> 00:06:57,106
One of the two who heard John and followed
him was Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother.

102
00:06:57,746 --> 00:07:03,306
He first found his own brother, Simon, and
said to him, “We have found the Messiah!”

103
00:07:04,026 --> 00:07:06,826
(which is, being interpreted, Christ).

104
00:07:07,986 --> 00:07:09,406
He brought him to Jesus.

105
00:07:10,426 --> 00:07:14,646
Jesus looked at him and said, “You are
Simon the son of Jonah.

106
00:07:15,406 --> 00:07:19,646
You shall be called Cephas” (which is by
interpretation, Peter).

107
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:25,790
On the next day, he was determined to go
out into Galilee, and he found Philip.

108
00:07:27,110 --> 00:07:29,670
Jesus said to him, “Follow me.”

109
00:07:30,530 --> 00:07:35,110
Now Philip was from Bethsaida, the city of
Andrew and Peter.

110
00:07:35,790 --> 00:07:42,290
Philip found Nathanael, and said to him, “We
have found him of whom Moses in the law

111
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:48,670
and also the prophets, wrote: Jesus of
Nazareth, the son of Joseph.”

112
00:07:48,710 --> 00:07:53,590
Nathanael said to him, “Can any good thing
come out of Nazareth?”

113
00:07:54,810 --> 00:07:57,190
Philip said to him, “Come and see.”

114
00:07:58,250 --> 00:08:04,670
Jesus saw Nathanael coming to him, and
said about him, “Behold, an Israelite indeed,

115
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:06,850
in whom is no deceit!”

116
00:08:06,890 --> 00:08:11,270
Nathanael said to him, “How do you know
me?”

117
00:08:11,970 --> 00:08:18,370
Jesus answered him, “Before Philip called you, when
you were under the fig tree, I saw

118
00:08:18,410 --> 00:08:18,710
you.”

119
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:23,830
Nathanael answered him, “Rabbi, you are
the Son of God!

120
00:08:24,630 --> 00:08:25,830
You are King of Israel!”

121
00:08:27,130 --> 00:08:33,410
Jesus answered him, “Because I told you, ‘I
saw you underneath the fig tree,’ do you

122
00:08:33,450 --> 00:08:34,350
believe?

123
00:08:34,810 --> 00:08:36,690
You will see greater things than these!”

124
00:08:37,470 --> 00:08:44,050
He said to him, “Most certainly, I tell
you all, hereafter you will see heaven opened,

125
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:48,570
and the angels of God ascending and
descending on the Son of Man.”

126
00:08:49,830 --> 00:08:51,830
John, chapter two.

127
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:55,970
The third day, there was a wedding in Cana
of Galilee.

128
00:08:56,550 --> 00:08:58,010
Jesus’ mother was there.

129
00:08:58,650 --> 00:09:02,530
Jesus also was invited, with his
disciples, to the wedding.

130
00:09:03,490 --> 00:09:09,450
When the wine ran out, Jesus’ mother said
to him, “They have no wine.”

131
00:09:10,290 --> 00:09:15,730
Jesus said to her, “Woman, what does that
have to do with you and me?

132
00:09:16,690 --> 00:09:18,450
My hour has not yet come.”

133
00:09:19,070 --> 00:09:23,510
His mother said to the servants, “Whatever
he says to you, do it.”

134
00:09:24,490 --> 00:09:31,370
Now there were six water pots of stone
set there after the Jews’ way of purifying, containing

135
00:09:31,410 --> 00:09:33,410
two or three metretes apiece.

136
00:09:34,670 --> 00:09:38,270
Jesus said to them, “Fill the water pots
with water.”

137
00:09:38,950 --> 00:09:40,690
So they filled them up to the brim.

138
00:09:41,430 --> 00:09:46,710
He said to them, “Now draw some out, and
take it to the ruler of the feast.”

139
00:09:47,730 --> 00:09:48,850
So they took it.

140
00:09:49,092 --> 00:09:55,052
When the ruler of the feast tasted the
water now become wine, and didn’t know where it

141
00:09:55,092 --> 00:10:01,452
came from (but the servants who had drawn
the water knew), the ruler of the feast called

142
00:10:01,492 --> 00:10:07,972
the bridegroom and said to him, “Everyone
serves the good wine first, and

143
00:10:08,012 --> 00:10:11,652
when the guests have drunk freely, then
that which is worse.

144
00:10:12,372 --> 00:10:14,672
You have kept the good wine until now!”

145
00:10:15,392 --> 00:10:22,752
This beginning of his signs Jesus did in
Cana of Galilee, and revealed his glory; and

146
00:10:22,792 --> 00:10:24,492
his disciples believed in him.

147
00:10:24,532 --> 00:10:31,152
After this, he went down to Capernaum, he,
and his mother, his brothers, and

148
00:10:31,192 --> 00:10:34,392
his disciples; and they stayed there a few
days.

149
00:10:35,112 --> 00:10:39,712
The Passover of the Jews was at hand, and
Jesus went up to Jerusalem.

150
00:10:40,612 --> 00:10:47,152
He found in the temple those who sold
oxen, sheep, and doves, and the changers of

151
00:10:47,192 --> 00:10:48,092
money sitting.

152
00:10:48,412 --> 00:10:54,572
He made a whip of cords and drove all
out of the temple, both the sheep and the oxen;

153
00:10:54,952 --> 00:10:59,032
and he poured out the changers’ money and
overthrew their tables.

154
00:10:59,972 --> 00:11:04,832
To those who sold the doves, he said,
“Take these things out of here!

155
00:11:05,592 --> 00:11:08,272
Don’t make my Father’s house a
marketplace!”

156
00:11:09,092 --> 00:11:15,172
His disciples remembered that it was written,
“Zeal for your house will eat me up.”

157
00:11:15,752 --> 00:11:21,312
The Jews therefore answered him, “What sign do
you show us, seeing that you do these

158
00:11:21,352 --> 00:11:22,252
things?”

159
00:11:22,892 --> 00:11:28,312
Jesus answered them, “Destroy this temple,
and in three days I will raise it up.”

160
00:11:29,292 --> 00:11:33,772
The Jews therefore said, “It took
forty-six years to build this temple!

161
00:11:34,572 --> 00:11:36,292
Will you raise it up in three days?”

162
00:11:36,332 --> 00:11:39,132
But he spoke of the temple of his body.

163
00:11:40,072 --> 00:11:45,592
When therefore he was raised from the
dead, his disciples remembered that he said this,

164
00:11:46,352 --> 00:11:50,352
and they believed the Scripture and the
word which Jesus had said.

165
00:11:50,972 --> 00:11:56,912
Now when he was in Jerusalem at the
Passover, during the feast, many believed in his

166
00:11:56,952 --> 00:11:59,872
name, observing his signs which he did.

167
00:12:00,672 --> 00:12:06,552
But Jesus didn’t entrust himself to them,
because he knew everyone, and because he didn’t

168
00:12:06,592 --> 00:12:12,352
need for anyone to testify concerning man;
for he himself knew what was in man.

169
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:14,820
John, chapter three.

170
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:19,980
Now there was a man of the Pharisees named
Nicodemus, a ruler of the Jews.

171
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:28,080
He came to Jesus by night and said to
him, “Rabbi, we know that you are a teacher come

172
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:34,400
from God, for no one can do these signs
that you do, unless God is with him.”

173
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:41,360
Jesus answered him, “Most certainly I tell
you, unless one is born anew, he

174
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,680
can’t see God’s Kingdom.”

175
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:48,560
Nicodemus said to him, “How can a man be
born when he is old?

176
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:53,240
Can he enter a second time into his
mother’s womb and be born?”

177
00:12:53,940 --> 00:13:00,900
Jesus answered, “Most certainly I tell you, unless
one is born of water and Spirit, he

178
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:02,640
can’t enter into God’s Kingdom.

179
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:06,020
That which is born of the flesh is flesh.

180
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:09,420
That which is born of the Spirit is
spirit.

181
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:13,860
Don’t marvel that I said to you, ‘You must
be born anew.’

182
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:20,380
The wind blows where it wants to, and you
hear its sound, but don’t know where it comes

183
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:22,020
from and where it is going.

184
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:25,440
So is everyone who is born of the Spirit.”

185
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:30,160
Nicodemus answered him, “How can these
things be?”

186
00:13:30,940 --> 00:13:36,560
Jesus answered him, “Are you the teacher
of Israel, and don’t understand these things?

187
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:43,460
Most certainly I tell you, we speak that which
we know and testify of that which we have

188
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:46,040
seen, and you don’t receive our witness.

189
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:52,140
If I told you earthly things and you don’t
believe, how will you believe if I tell you

190
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:53,080
heavenly things?

191
00:13:54,140 --> 00:14:00,640
No one has ascended into heaven but he who
descended out of heaven, the Son of Man, who

192
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:01,580
is in heaven.

193
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:07,960
As Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness,
even so must the Son of Man be lifted

194
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:13,380
up, that whoever believes in him should
not perish, but have eternal life.

195
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:20,600
For God so loved the world, that he
gave his only born Son, that whoever believes in

196
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:23,580
him should not perish, but have eternal
life.

197
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:30,240
For God didn’t send his Son into the world
to judge the world, but that the world should

198
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:31,680
be saved through him.

199
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:35,300
He who believes in him is not judged.

200
00:14:35,858 --> 00:14:42,518
He who doesn’t believe has been judged already,
because he has not believed in the name

201
00:14:42,558 --> 00:14:44,638
of the only born Son of God.

202
00:14:45,378 --> 00:14:51,458
This is the judgement, that the light has
come into the world, and men loved the darkness

203
00:14:51,498 --> 00:14:55,078
rather than the light, for their works
were evil.

204
00:14:55,738 --> 00:15:01,998
For everyone who does evil hates the light
and doesn’t come to the light, lest his works

205
00:15:02,038 --> 00:15:03,018
would be exposed.

206
00:15:03,858 --> 00:15:10,498
But he who does the truth comes to the
light, that his works may be revealed, that they

207
00:15:10,538 --> 00:15:11,778
have been done in God.”

208
00:15:12,298 --> 00:15:17,398
After these things, Jesus came with his
disciples into the land of Judea.

209
00:15:17,878 --> 00:15:21,358
He stayed there with them and baptised.

210
00:15:21,398 --> 00:15:27,258
John also was baptising in Enon near
Salim, because there was much water there.

211
00:15:28,378 --> 00:15:33,538
They came and were baptised; for John was
not yet thrown into prison.

212
00:15:33,958 --> 00:15:39,838
Therefore a dispute arose on the part
of John’s disciples with some Jews about purification.

213
00:15:40,798 --> 00:15:48,038
They came to John and said to him, “Rabbi,
he who was with you beyond the Jordan, to

214
00:15:48,078 --> 00:15:54,138
whom you have testified, behold, he
baptises, and everyone is coming to him.”

215
00:15:54,938 --> 00:16:00,618
John answered, “A man can receive nothing
unless it has been given him from heaven.

216
00:16:01,378 --> 00:16:08,158
You yourselves testify that I said, ‘I am
not the Christ,’ but, ‘I have been sent before

217
00:16:08,198 --> 00:16:09,098
him.’

218
00:16:09,358 --> 00:16:15,098
He who has the bride is the bridegroom;
but the friend of the bridegroom, who stands

219
00:16:15,138 --> 00:16:19,778
and hears him, rejoices greatly because of
the bridegroom’s voice.

220
00:16:20,558 --> 00:16:22,658
Therefore my joy is made full.

221
00:16:23,338 --> 00:16:26,118
He must increase, but I must decrease.

222
00:16:27,638 --> 00:16:30,358
“He who comes from above is above all.

223
00:16:31,158 --> 00:16:35,858
He who is from the earth belongs to the
earth and speaks of the earth.

224
00:16:36,878 --> 00:16:39,478
He who comes from heaven is above all.

225
00:16:40,298 --> 00:16:46,258
What he has seen and heard, of that
he testifies; and no one receives his witness.

226
00:16:46,998 --> 00:16:52,538
He who has received his witness has set
his seal to this, that God is true.

227
00:16:53,558 --> 00:17:00,238
For he whom God has sent speaks the words
of God; for God gives the Spirit without measure.

228
00:17:01,458 --> 00:17:05,818
The Father loves the Son, and has given
all things into his hand.

229
00:17:06,155 --> 00:17:12,875
One who believes in the Son has eternal
life, but one who disobeys the Son won’t

230
00:17:12,915 --> 00:17:16,515
see life, but the wrath of God remains on
him.”

231
00:17:17,555 --> 00:17:19,675
John, chapter four.

232
00:17:19,715 --> 00:17:25,835
Therefore when the Lord knew that the Pharisees
had heard that Jesus was making and baptising

233
00:17:25,875 --> 00:17:31,955
more disciples than John (although Jesus
himself didn’t baptise, but his disciples),

234
00:17:31,995 --> 00:17:36,255
he left Judea and departed into Galilee.

235
00:17:36,835 --> 00:17:39,015
He needed to pass through Samaria.

236
00:17:39,515 --> 00:17:46,075
So he came to a city of Samaria called
Sychar, near the parcel of ground that Jacob gave

237
00:17:46,115 --> 00:17:47,275
to his son Joseph.

238
00:17:48,435 --> 00:17:49,935
Jacob’s well was there.

239
00:17:50,375 --> 00:17:55,055
Jesus therefore, being tired from his
journey, sat down by the well.

240
00:17:55,975 --> 00:17:57,655
It was about the sixth hour.

241
00:17:58,135 --> 00:18:00,755
A woman of Samaria came to draw water.

242
00:18:00,795 --> 00:18:03,915
Jesus said to her, “Give me a drink.”

243
00:18:04,915 --> 00:18:08,555
For his disciples had gone away into the
city to buy food.

244
00:18:09,635 --> 00:18:16,155
The Samaritan woman therefore said to him,
“How is it that you, being a Jew, ask for

245
00:18:16,195 --> 00:18:18,555
a drink from me, a Samaritan woman?”

246
00:18:19,375 --> 00:18:25,915
(For Jews have no dealings with Samaritans.)
Jesus answered her, “If you knew the gift

247
00:18:25,955 --> 00:18:32,815
of God, and who it is who says to you,
‘Give me a drink,’ you would have asked him, and

248
00:18:32,855 --> 00:18:34,615
he would have given you living water.”

249
00:18:35,615 --> 00:18:41,555
The woman said to him, “Sir, you have
nothing to draw with, and the well is deep.

250
00:18:42,215 --> 00:18:44,115
So where do you get that living water?

251
00:18:44,995 --> 00:18:50,495
Are you greater than our father Jacob, who
gave us the well and drank from it himself,

252
00:18:51,515 --> 00:18:53,495
as did his children and his livestock?”

253
00:18:54,275 --> 00:19:00,895
Jesus answered her, “Everyone who drinks of
this water will thirst again, but whoever

254
00:19:00,935 --> 00:19:06,835
drinks of the water that I will give
him will never thirst again; but the water that

255
00:19:06,875 --> 00:19:11,955
I will give him will become in him a well
of water springing up to eternal life.”

256
00:19:12,575 --> 00:19:19,755
The woman said to him, “Sir, give me
this water, so that I don’t get thirsty, neither

257
00:19:19,795 --> 00:19:21,775
come all the way here to draw.”

258
00:19:21,815 --> 00:19:27,735
Jesus said to her, “Go, call your husband,
and come here.”

259
00:19:28,755 --> 00:19:31,415
The woman answered, “I have no husband.”

260
00:19:31,850 --> 00:19:38,330
Jesus said to her, “You said well, ‘I have
no husband,’ for you have

261
00:19:38,370 --> 00:19:43,210
had five husbands; and he whom you now
have is not your husband.

262
00:19:44,010 --> 00:19:45,730
This you have said truly.”

263
00:19:47,130 --> 00:19:52,130
The woman said to him, “Sir, I perceive
that you are a prophet.

264
00:19:52,730 --> 00:19:58,550
Our fathers worshipped in this mountain, and you
Jews say that in Jerusalem is the place

265
00:19:58,590 --> 00:20:00,110
where people ought to worship.”

266
00:20:01,010 --> 00:20:07,510
Jesus said to her, “Woman, believe me, the
hour is coming when neither in

267
00:20:07,550 --> 00:20:10,970
this mountain nor in Jerusalem will you
worship the Father.

268
00:20:11,870 --> 00:20:13,930
You worship that which you don’t know.

269
00:20:14,510 --> 00:20:18,490
We worship that which we know; for
salvation is from the Jews.

270
00:20:19,650 --> 00:20:25,490
But the hour comes, and now is, when
the true worshippers will worship the Father in

271
00:20:25,530 --> 00:20:30,570
spirit and truth, for the Father seeks
such to be his worshippers.

272
00:20:30,610 --> 00:20:35,450
God is spirit, and those who worship him
must worship in spirit and truth.”

273
00:20:36,190 --> 00:20:42,090
The woman said to him, “I know that
Messiah is coming, he who is called Christ.

274
00:20:43,130 --> 00:20:46,630
When he has come, he will declare to us
all things.”

275
00:20:47,630 --> 00:20:52,470
Jesus said to her, “I am he, the one who
speaks to you.”

276
00:20:52,830 --> 00:20:55,150
Just then, his disciples came.

277
00:20:56,050 --> 00:21:01,770
They marvelled that he was speaking with a
woman; yet no one said, “What are you looking

278
00:21:01,810 --> 00:21:02,710
for?”

279
00:21:02,990 --> 00:21:05,050
or, “Why do you speak with her?”

280
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:12,670
So the woman left her water pot, went away
into the city, and said to the people, “Come,

281
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:16,290
see a man who told me everything that I
have done.

282
00:21:17,210 --> 00:21:18,230
Can this be the Christ?”

283
00:21:19,030 --> 00:21:21,790
They went out of the city, and were coming
to him.

284
00:21:22,590 --> 00:21:28,110
In the meanwhile, the disciples urged him,
saying, “Rabbi, eat.”

285
00:21:29,150 --> 00:21:33,170
But he said to them, “I have food to eat
that you don’t know about.”

286
00:21:34,150 --> 00:21:39,410
The disciples therefore said to one another,
“Has anyone brought him something to eat?”

287
00:21:40,070 --> 00:21:46,430
Jesus said to them, “My food is to do the
will of him who sent me and to accomplish his

288
00:21:46,470 --> 00:21:47,370
work.

289
00:21:47,690 --> 00:21:51,650
Don’t you say, ‘There are yet four months
until the harvest?’

290
00:21:52,810 --> 00:21:58,690
Behold, I tell you, lift up your eyes and
look at the fields, that they are white for

291
00:21:58,730 --> 00:21:59,670
harvest already.

292
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:06,680
He who reaps receives wages and gathers
fruit to eternal life, that both he

293
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:10,320
who sows and he who reaps may rejoice
together.

294
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:16,600
For in this the saying is true, ‘One sows,
and another reaps.’

295
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:21,580
I sent you to reap that for which you
haven’t laboured.

296
00:22:21,620 --> 00:22:25,900
Others have laboured, and you have entered
into their labour.”

297
00:22:25,940 --> 00:22:31,600
From that city many of the Samaritans believed
in him because of the word of the woman,

298
00:22:32,180 --> 00:22:35,920
who testified, “He told me everything that
I have done.”

299
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:41,380
So when the Samaritans came to him, they
begged him to stay with them.

300
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:43,260
He stayed there two days.

301
00:22:43,980 --> 00:22:46,300
Many more believed because of his word.

302
00:22:47,260 --> 00:22:53,400
They said to the woman, “Now we believe,
not because of your speaking; for we have heard

303
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:58,800
for ourselves, and know that this is
indeed the Christ, the Saviour of the world.”

304
00:22:59,260 --> 00:23:03,600
After the two days he went out from there
and went into Galilee.

305
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:09,800
For Jesus himself testified that a prophet
has no honour in his own country.

306
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:16,540
So when he came into Galilee, the
Galileans received him, having seen all the things

307
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:21,060
that he did in Jerusalem at the feast, for
they also went to the feast.

308
00:23:22,140 --> 00:23:27,940
Jesus came therefore again to Cana of
Galilee, where he made the water into wine.

309
00:23:28,660 --> 00:23:32,200
There was a certain nobleman whose son was
sick at Capernaum.

310
00:23:33,020 --> 00:23:39,420
When he heard that Jesus had come out of
Judea into Galilee, he went to him and begged

311
00:23:39,460 --> 00:23:44,420
him that he would come down and heal his
son, for he was at the point of death.

312
00:23:45,020 --> 00:23:51,380
Jesus therefore said to him, “Unless you see
signs and wonders, you will in no way believe.”

313
00:23:52,540 --> 00:23:57,760
The nobleman said to him, “Sir, come down
before my child dies.”

314
00:23:58,820 --> 00:24:01,260
Jesus said to him, “Go your way.

315
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:02,660
Your son lives.”

316
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:08,240
The man believed the word that Jesus spoke
to him, and he went his way.

317
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:15,520
As he was going down, his servants met him
and reported, saying “Your child lives!”

318
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:20,880
So he enquired of them the hour when he
began to get better.

319
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:27,940
They said therefore to him, “Yesterday at
the seventh hour, the fever left him.”

320
00:24:28,195 --> 00:24:34,715
So the father knew that it was at that
hour in which Jesus said to him, “Your son lives.”

321
00:24:35,755 --> 00:24:38,515
He believed, as did his whole house.

322
00:24:39,435 --> 00:24:46,175
This is again the second sign that Jesus
did, having come out of Judea into Galilee.

323
00:24:47,275 --> 00:24:48,975
John, chapter five.

324
00:24:49,015 --> 00:24:54,495
After these things, there was a feast of
the Jews, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem.

325
00:24:55,675 --> 00:25:02,215
Now in Jerusalem by the sheep gate, there
is a pool, which is called in Hebrew, “Bethesda”,

326
00:25:03,115 --> 00:25:04,355
having five porches.

327
00:25:04,395 --> 00:25:11,595
In these lay a great multitude of those
who were sick, blind, lame, or paralysed,

328
00:25:11,635 --> 00:25:17,215
waiting for the moving of the water; for
an angel went down at certain times into the

329
00:25:17,255 --> 00:25:19,195
pool and stirred up the water.

330
00:25:20,035 --> 00:25:25,975
Whoever stepped in first after the stirring
of the water was healed of whatever disease

331
00:25:26,015 --> 00:25:26,915
he had.

332
00:25:27,295 --> 00:25:31,375
A certain man was there who had been sick
for thirty-eight years.

333
00:25:32,375 --> 00:25:38,955
When Jesus saw him lying there, and knew that
he had been sick for a long time, he asked

334
00:25:38,995 --> 00:25:41,795
him, “Do you want to be made well?”

335
00:25:42,275 --> 00:25:48,375
The sick man answered him, “Sir, I have no
one to put me into the pool when the water

336
00:25:48,415 --> 00:25:53,515
is stirred up, but while I’m coming,
another steps down before me.”

337
00:25:54,375 --> 00:25:58,855
Jesus said to him, “Arise, take up your
mat, and walk.”

338
00:25:58,895 --> 00:26:04,035
Immediately, the man was made well, and
took up his mat and walked.

339
00:26:04,565 --> 00:26:06,315
Now that day was a Sabbath.

340
00:26:07,295 --> 00:26:11,775
So the Jews said to him who was cured, “It
is the Sabbath.

341
00:26:12,675 --> 00:26:15,175
It is not lawful for you to carry the
mat.”

342
00:26:16,055 --> 00:26:23,275
He answered them, “He who made me well said
to me, ‘Take up your mat and walk.’” Then

343
00:26:23,315 --> 00:26:28,615
they asked him, “Who is the man who said
to you, ‘Take up your mat and walk’?”

344
00:26:29,735 --> 00:26:36,695
But he who was healed didn’t know who
it was, for Jesus had withdrawn, a crowd being

345
00:26:36,735 --> 00:26:37,635
in the place.

346
00:26:37,875 --> 00:26:43,895
Afterward Jesus found him in the temple and
said to him, “Behold, you are made well.

347
00:26:44,835 --> 00:26:48,355
Sin no more, so that nothing worse happens
to you.”

348
00:26:49,195 --> 00:26:54,535
The man went away, and told the Jews that
it was Jesus who had made him well.

349
00:26:54,859 --> 00:27:00,999
For this cause the Jews persecuted Jesus and
sought to kill him, because he did these

350
00:27:01,039 --> 00:27:02,139
things on the Sabbath.

351
00:27:03,319 --> 00:27:09,539
But Jesus answered them, “My Father is
still working, so I am working, too.”

352
00:27:10,059 --> 00:27:15,699
For this cause therefore the Jews sought all
the more to kill him, because he not only

353
00:27:15,739 --> 00:27:22,519
broke the Sabbath, but also called God his
own Father, making himself equal with

354
00:27:22,559 --> 00:27:23,319
God.

355
00:27:23,359 --> 00:27:29,799
Jesus therefore answered them, “Most certainly, I
tell you, the Son can do nothing of

356
00:27:29,839 --> 00:27:32,979
himself, but what he sees the Father
doing.

357
00:27:33,539 --> 00:27:37,959
For whatever things he does, these the Son
also does likewise.

358
00:27:38,719 --> 00:27:44,499
For the Father has affection for the Son,
and shows him all things that he himself does.

359
00:27:45,039 --> 00:27:48,839
He will show him greater works than these,
that you may marvel.

360
00:27:49,859 --> 00:27:56,559
For as the Father raises the dead and
gives them life, even so the Son also gives

361
00:27:56,599 --> 00:27:58,219
life to whom he desires.

362
00:27:58,959 --> 00:28:05,039
For the Father judges no one, but he has
given all judgement to the Son, that all may

363
00:28:05,079 --> 00:28:08,279
honour the Son, even as they honour the
Father.

364
00:28:09,039 --> 00:28:13,679
He who doesn’t honour the Son doesn’t
honour the Father who sent him.

365
00:28:14,139 --> 00:28:20,899
“Most certainly I tell you, he who hears
my word and believes him who sent me has

366
00:28:20,939 --> 00:28:26,999
eternal life, and doesn’t come into judgement,
but has passed out of death into life.

367
00:28:28,039 --> 00:28:34,719
Most certainly I tell you, the hour comes, and
now is, when the dead will hear the Son

368
00:28:34,759 --> 00:28:37,779
of God’s voice; and those who hear will
live.

369
00:28:38,679 --> 00:28:45,219
For as the Father has life in himself,
even so he gave to the Son also to have

370
00:28:45,259 --> 00:28:46,159
life in himself.

371
00:28:46,879 --> 00:28:52,399
He also gave him authority to execute
judgement, because he is a son of man.

372
00:28:52,999 --> 00:28:58,819
Don’t marvel at this, for the hour comes in
which all who are in the tombs will hear

373
00:28:58,859 --> 00:29:05,739
his voice and will come out; those who
have done good, to the resurrection of life; and

374
00:29:05,779 --> 00:29:09,739
those who have done evil, to the
resurrection of judgement.

375
00:29:09,779 --> 00:29:11,879
I can of myself do nothing.

376
00:29:12,659 --> 00:29:19,139
As I hear, I judge; and my judgement is
righteous, because I don’t seek my own

377
00:29:19,179 --> 00:29:22,879
will, but the will of my Father who sent
me.

378
00:29:23,165 --> 00:29:27,345
“If I testify about myself, my witness is
not valid.

379
00:29:28,405 --> 00:29:30,825
It is another who testifies about me.

380
00:29:31,705 --> 00:29:35,665
I know that the testimony which he
testifies about me is true.

381
00:29:36,345 --> 00:29:40,265
You have sent to John, and he has
testified to the truth.

382
00:29:41,165 --> 00:29:44,185
But the testimony which I receive is not
from man.

383
00:29:44,825 --> 00:29:48,125
However, I say these things that you may
be saved.

384
00:29:48,905 --> 00:29:54,565
He was the burning and shining lamp, and you
were willing to rejoice for a while in his

385
00:29:54,605 --> 00:29:55,505
light.

386
00:29:55,885 --> 00:30:00,965
But the testimony which I have is greater
than that of John; for the works which the

387
00:30:01,005 --> 00:30:07,965
Father gave me to accomplish, the very
works that I do, testify about me, that

388
00:30:08,005 --> 00:30:09,245
the Father has sent me.

389
00:30:09,825 --> 00:30:14,425
The Father himself, who sent me, has
testified about me.

390
00:30:14,845 --> 00:30:18,965
You have neither heard his voice at any
time, nor seen his form.

391
00:30:19,685 --> 00:30:24,525
You don’t have his word living in you,
because you don’t believe him whom he sent.

392
00:30:25,545 --> 00:30:31,225
“You search the Scriptures, because you think
that in them you have eternal life; and

393
00:30:31,265 --> 00:30:33,545
these are they which testify about me.

394
00:30:34,425 --> 00:30:37,405
Yet you will not come to me, that you may
have life.

395
00:30:38,165 --> 00:30:40,065
I don’t receive glory from men.

396
00:30:40,545 --> 00:30:44,265
But I know you, that you don’t have God’s
love in yourselves.

397
00:30:44,965 --> 00:30:49,145
I have come in my Father’s name, and you
don’t receive me.

398
00:30:50,065 --> 00:30:53,625
If another comes in his own name, you will
receive him.

399
00:30:54,265 --> 00:30:59,945
How can you believe, who receive glory from
one another, and you don’t seek the glory

400
00:30:59,985 --> 00:31:01,685
that comes from the only God?

401
00:31:02,725 --> 00:31:05,485
“Don’t think that I will accuse you to the
Father.

402
00:31:06,265 --> 00:31:11,645
There is one who accuses you, even Moses,
on whom you have set your hope.

403
00:31:12,465 --> 00:31:17,205
For if you believed Moses, you would
believe me; for he wrote about me.

404
00:31:18,045 --> 00:31:22,205
But if you don’t believe his writings, how
will you believe my words?”

405
00:31:23,165 --> 00:31:25,665
John, chapter six.

406
00:31:25,705 --> 00:31:32,045
After these things, Jesus went away to the
other side of the sea of Galilee, which is

407
00:31:32,085 --> 00:31:34,825
also called the Sea of Tiberias.

408
00:31:34,865 --> 00:31:40,885
A great multitude followed him, because they saw
his signs which he did on those who

409
00:31:40,925 --> 00:31:41,825
were sick.

410
00:31:42,445 --> 00:31:46,625
Jesus went up into the mountain, and he
sat there with his disciples.

411
00:31:47,216 --> 00:31:51,256
Now the Passover, the feast of the Jews,
was at hand.

412
00:31:52,416 --> 00:31:58,077
Jesus therefore, lifting up his eyes and
seeing that a great multitude was coming to

413
00:31:58,116 --> 00:32:04,116
him, said to Philip, “Where are we to buy
bread, that these may eat?”

414
00:32:05,136 --> 00:32:09,516
He said this to test him, for he himself
knew what he would do.

415
00:32:10,216 --> 00:32:15,996
Philip answered him, “Two hundred denarii
worth of bread is not sufficient for them,

416
00:32:16,036 --> 00:32:18,876
that every one of them may receive a
little.”

417
00:32:19,496 --> 00:32:26,016
One of his disciples, Andrew, Simon Peter’s brother,
said to him, “There is a boy here

418
00:32:26,056 --> 00:32:32,496
who has five barley loaves and two fish,
but what are these amongst so many?”

419
00:32:33,436 --> 00:32:36,316
Jesus said, “Have the people sit down.”

420
00:32:36,876 --> 00:32:39,476
Now there was much grass in that place.

421
00:32:39,956 --> 00:32:43,836
So the men sat down, in number about five
thousand.

422
00:32:44,776 --> 00:32:51,516
Jesus took the loaves, and having given
thanks, he distributed to the disciples, and

423
00:32:51,556 --> 00:32:57,276
the disciples to those who were sitting down,
likewise also of the fish as much as they

424
00:32:57,316 --> 00:32:58,216
desired.

425
00:32:58,516 --> 00:33:04,236
When they were filled, he said to his
disciples, “Gather up the broken pieces which are

426
00:33:04,276 --> 00:33:06,636
left over, that nothing be lost.”

427
00:33:07,496 --> 00:33:12,976
So they gathered them up, and filled
twelve baskets with broken pieces from the five

428
00:33:13,016 --> 00:33:16,516
barley loaves, which were left over by
those who had eaten.

429
00:33:17,236 --> 00:33:23,876
When therefore the people saw the sign which
Jesus did, they said, “This is truly the

430
00:33:23,916 --> 00:33:25,956
prophet who comes into the world.”

431
00:33:26,996 --> 00:33:32,196
Jesus therefore, perceiving that they were about to
come and take him by force to make

432
00:33:32,236 --> 00:33:36,016
him king, withdrew again to the mountain
by himself.

433
00:33:36,756 --> 00:33:40,096
When evening came, his disciples went down
to the sea.

434
00:33:40,756 --> 00:33:45,256
They entered into the boat, and were going
over the sea to Capernaum.

435
00:33:45,896 --> 00:33:49,536
It was now dark, and Jesus had not come to
them.

436
00:33:50,276 --> 00:33:53,156
The sea was tossed by a great wind
blowing.

437
00:33:53,896 --> 00:33:59,976
When therefore they had rowed about twenty-five
or thirty stadia, they saw Jesus walking

438
00:34:00,016 --> 00:34:04,476
on the sea and drawing near to the boat;
and they were afraid.

439
00:34:05,536 --> 00:34:07,696
But he said to them, “It is I.

440
00:34:08,396 --> 00:34:09,316
Don’t be afraid.”

441
00:34:10,216 --> 00:34:13,396
They were willing therefore to receive him
into the boat.

442
00:34:13,737 --> 00:34:16,997
Immediately the boat was at the land where
they were going.

443
00:34:17,717 --> 00:34:22,857
On the next day, the multitude that stood on
the other side of the sea saw that there

444
00:34:22,897 --> 00:34:29,417
was no other boat there, except the one in
which his disciples had embarked, and that

445
00:34:29,457 --> 00:34:35,277
Jesus hadn’t entered with his disciples into
the boat, but his disciples had gone away

446
00:34:35,317 --> 00:34:36,217
alone.

447
00:34:36,437 --> 00:34:42,157
However, boats from Tiberias came near to the
place where they ate the bread after the

448
00:34:42,197 --> 00:34:43,337
Lord had given thanks.

449
00:34:44,517 --> 00:34:50,797
When the multitude therefore saw that Jesus
wasn’t there, nor his disciples, they themselves

450
00:34:50,837 --> 00:34:55,277
got into the boats and came to Capernaum,
seeking Jesus.

451
00:34:56,017 --> 00:35:02,177
When they found him on the other side of
the sea, they asked him, “Rabbi, when did you

452
00:35:02,217 --> 00:35:03,117
come here?”

453
00:35:03,757 --> 00:35:10,457
Jesus answered them, “Most certainly I
tell you, you seek me, not because

454
00:35:10,497 --> 00:35:14,737
you saw signs, but because you ate of the
loaves and were filled.

455
00:35:15,397 --> 00:35:21,197
Don’t work for the food which perishes, but
for the food which remains to eternal life,

456
00:35:21,977 --> 00:35:24,197
which the Son of Man will give to you.

457
00:35:25,157 --> 00:35:27,197
For God the Father has sealed him.”

458
00:35:27,977 --> 00:35:33,937
They said therefore to him, “What must we
do, that we may work the works of God?”

459
00:35:34,617 --> 00:35:41,197
Jesus answered them, “This is the work of
God, that you believe in him whom he has

460
00:35:41,237 --> 00:35:42,137
sent.”

461
00:35:42,597 --> 00:35:49,137
They said therefore to him, “What then do
you do for a sign, that we may see and

462
00:35:49,177 --> 00:35:50,077
believe you?

463
00:35:50,677 --> 00:35:51,957
What work do you do?

464
00:35:52,717 --> 00:35:55,337
Our fathers ate the manna in the
wilderness.

465
00:35:56,077 --> 00:36:02,517
As it is written, ‘He gave them bread
out of heaven to eat.’” Jesus therefore said to

466
00:36:02,557 --> 00:36:08,857
them, “Most certainly, I tell you, it wasn’t
Moses who gave you the bread out of heaven,

467
00:36:09,277 --> 00:36:12,657
but my Father gives you the true bread out
of heaven.

468
00:36:13,057 --> 00:36:18,577
For the bread of God is that which comes
down out of heaven and gives life to the world.”

469
00:36:19,917 --> 00:36:24,537
They said therefore to him, “Lord, always
give us this bread.”

470
00:36:25,557 --> 00:36:28,737
Jesus said to them, “I am the bread of
life.

471
00:36:29,737 --> 00:36:35,177
Whoever comes to me will not be hungry,
and whoever believes in me will never be thirsty.

472
00:36:35,734 --> 00:36:39,634
But I told you that you have seen me, and
yet you don’t believe.

473
00:36:40,694 --> 00:36:44,034
All those whom the Father gives me will
come to me.

474
00:36:44,934 --> 00:36:47,974
He who comes to me I will in no way throw
out.

475
00:36:49,074 --> 00:36:54,754
For I have come down from heaven, not to do
my own will, but the will of him who sent

476
00:36:54,794 --> 00:36:55,634
me.

477
00:36:55,674 --> 00:37:01,454
This is the will of my Father who sent me,
that of all he has given to me I should lose

478
00:37:01,494 --> 00:37:04,914
nothing, but should raise him up at the
last day.

479
00:37:05,834 --> 00:37:11,434
This is the will of the one who sent
me, that everyone who sees the Son and believes

480
00:37:11,474 --> 00:37:16,434
in him should have eternal life; and I
will raise him up at the last day.”

481
00:37:17,094 --> 00:37:23,134
The Jews therefore murmured concerning him, because
he said, “I am the bread which came

482
00:37:23,174 --> 00:37:24,174
down out of heaven.”

483
00:37:25,134 --> 00:37:31,194
They said, “Isn’t this Jesus, the son of
Joseph, whose father and mother we know?

484
00:37:31,794 --> 00:37:37,794
How then does he say, ‘I have come
down out of heaven?’” Therefore Jesus answered them,

485
00:37:38,474 --> 00:37:40,214
“Don’t murmur amongst yourselves.

486
00:37:41,294 --> 00:37:47,234
No one can come to me unless the Father who
sent me draws him; and I will raise him up

487
00:37:47,274 --> 00:37:48,214
in the last day.

488
00:37:49,294 --> 00:37:53,214
It is written in the prophets, ‘They will
all be taught by God.’

489
00:37:53,974 --> 00:37:58,474
Therefore everyone who hears from the
Father and has learnt, comes to me.

490
00:37:59,234 --> 00:38:03,674
Not that anyone has seen the Father,
except he who is from God.

491
00:38:04,534 --> 00:38:05,634
He has seen the Father.

492
00:38:06,494 --> 00:38:11,434
Most certainly, I tell you, he who
believes in me has eternal life.

493
00:38:12,254 --> 00:38:13,354
I am the bread of life.

494
00:38:14,234 --> 00:38:17,434
Your fathers ate the manna in the
wilderness and they died.

495
00:38:18,474 --> 00:38:24,414
This is the bread which comes down out of
heaven, that anyone may eat of it and not die.

496
00:38:25,274 --> 00:38:28,474
I am the living bread which came down out
of heaven.

497
00:38:29,354 --> 00:38:32,514
If anyone eats of this bread, he will live
forever.

498
00:38:33,354 --> 00:38:37,794
Yes, the bread which I will give for the
life of the world is my flesh.”

499
00:38:39,034 --> 00:38:44,594
The Jews therefore contended with one another,
saying, “How can this man give us his

500
00:38:44,634 --> 00:38:45,534
flesh to eat?”

501
00:38:46,234 --> 00:38:52,854
Jesus therefore said to them, “Most certainly I
tell you, unless you eat the flesh of

502
00:38:52,894 --> 00:38:57,254
the Son of Man and drink his blood, you
don’t have life in yourselves.

503
00:38:57,943 --> 00:39:04,483
He who eats my flesh and drinks my blood
has eternal life, and I will raise

504
00:39:04,523 --> 00:39:06,203
him up at the last day.

505
00:39:07,123 --> 00:39:12,083
For my flesh is food indeed, and my blood
is drink indeed.

506
00:39:13,043 --> 00:39:19,443
He who eats my flesh and drinks my blood
lives in me, and I in him.

507
00:39:20,063 --> 00:39:26,603
As the living Father sent me, and I live
because of the Father, so he who feeds on

508
00:39:26,643 --> 00:39:29,443
me will also live because of me.

509
00:39:30,443 --> 00:39:36,563
This is the bread which came down out
of heaven—not as our fathers ate the manna and

510
00:39:36,603 --> 00:39:37,403
died.

511
00:39:37,443 --> 00:39:40,103
He who eats this bread will live forever.”

512
00:39:40,963 --> 00:39:44,963
He said these things in the synagogue, as
he taught in Capernaum.

513
00:39:45,803 --> 00:39:51,683
Therefore many of his disciples, when they
heard this, said, “This is a hard saying!

514
00:39:51,723 --> 00:39:53,503
Who can listen to it?”

515
00:39:53,803 --> 00:40:00,443
But Jesus knowing in himself that his
disciples murmured at this, said to them, “Does

516
00:40:00,483 --> 00:40:01,843
this cause you to stumble?

517
00:40:02,743 --> 00:40:06,983
Then what if you would see the Son of Man
ascending to where he was before?

518
00:40:08,003 --> 00:40:09,703
It is the spirit who gives life.

519
00:40:09,743 --> 00:40:12,003
The flesh profits nothing.

520
00:40:13,043 --> 00:40:16,743
The words that I speak to you are spirit,
and are life.

521
00:40:17,323 --> 00:40:19,583
But there are some of you who don’t
believe.”

522
00:40:20,303 --> 00:40:25,943
For Jesus knew from the beginning who they
were who didn’t believe, and who it was who

523
00:40:25,983 --> 00:40:26,883
would betray him.

524
00:40:27,643 --> 00:40:33,743
He said, “For this cause I have said to you
that no one can come to me, unless it is

525
00:40:33,783 --> 00:40:35,463
given to him by my Father.”

526
00:40:35,843 --> 00:40:40,483
At this, many of his disciples went back
and walked no more with him.

527
00:40:41,023 --> 00:40:46,503
Jesus said therefore to the twelve, “You
don’t also want to go away, do you?”

528
00:40:47,403 --> 00:40:51,723
Simon Peter answered him, “Lord, to whom
would we go?

529
00:40:52,623 --> 00:40:54,543
You have the words of eternal life.

530
00:40:55,403 --> 00:41:00,743
We have come to believe and know that you
are the Christ, the Son of the living God.”

531
00:41:01,383 --> 00:41:06,963
Jesus answered them, “Didn’t I choose you,
the twelve, and one of you is a devil?”

532
00:41:07,783 --> 00:41:14,383
Now he spoke of Judas, the son of Simon
Iscariot, for it was he who would betray him,

533
00:41:14,783 --> 00:41:16,023
being one of the twelve.

534
00:41:16,663 --> 00:41:18,083
John, chapter seven.

535
00:41:18,643 --> 00:41:25,483
After these things, Jesus was walking in
Galilee, for he wouldn’t walk in Judea, because

536
00:41:25,523 --> 00:41:27,243
the Jews sought to kill him.

537
00:41:27,523 --> 00:41:32,143
Now the feast of the Jews, the Feast of
Booths, was at hand.

538
00:41:33,303 --> 00:41:39,923
His brothers therefore said to him, “Depart from
here and go into Judea, that your disciples

539
00:41:39,963 --> 00:41:42,623
also may see your works which you do.

540
00:41:43,423 --> 00:41:47,843
For no one does anything in secret while
he seeks to be known openly.

541
00:41:48,703 --> 00:41:51,963
If you do these things, reveal yourself to
the world.”

542
00:41:53,143 --> 00:41:55,423
For even his brothers didn’t believe in
him.

543
00:41:56,223 --> 00:42:03,163
Jesus therefore said to them, “My time has
not yet come, but your time is always ready.

544
00:42:04,143 --> 00:42:10,503
The world can’t hate you, but it hates me,
because I testify about it, that its works

545
00:42:10,543 --> 00:42:11,443
are evil.

546
00:42:11,923 --> 00:42:12,903
You go up to the feast.

547
00:42:13,703 --> 00:42:18,503
I am not yet going up to this feast,
because my time is not yet fulfilled.”

548
00:42:19,923 --> 00:42:23,543
Having said these things to them, he
stayed in Galilee.

549
00:42:24,063 --> 00:42:30,503
But when his brothers had gone up to the
feast, then he also went up, not publicly, but

550
00:42:30,543 --> 00:42:31,703
as it were in secret.

551
00:42:32,543 --> 00:42:37,363
The Jews therefore sought him at the
feast, and said, “Where is he?”

552
00:42:38,303 --> 00:42:42,043
There was much murmuring amongst the
multitudes concerning him.

553
00:42:42,943 --> 00:42:45,203
Some said, “He is a good man.”

554
00:42:46,263 --> 00:42:50,743
Others said, “Not so, but he leads the
multitude astray.”

555
00:42:51,523 --> 00:42:55,143
Yet no one spoke openly of him for fear of
the Jews.

556
00:42:55,863 --> 00:43:01,443
But when it was now the middle of the
feast, Jesus went up into the temple and taught.

557
00:43:02,523 --> 00:43:08,883
The Jews therefore marvelled, saying, “How does
this man know letters, having never been

558
00:43:08,923 --> 00:43:09,823
educated?”

559
00:43:10,703 --> 00:43:16,623
Jesus therefore answered them, “My
teaching is not mine, but his who sent me.

560
00:43:17,083 --> 00:43:23,123
If anyone desires to do his will, he
will know about the teaching, whether it is from

561
00:43:23,163 --> 00:43:25,603
God or if I am speaking from myself.

562
00:43:27,283 --> 00:43:33,743
He who speaks from himself seeks his own glory,
but he who seeks the glory of him who

563
00:43:33,783 --> 00:43:37,803
sent him is true, and no unrighteousness
is in him.

564
00:43:38,323 --> 00:43:42,483
Didn’t Moses give you the law, and yet
none of you keeps the law?

565
00:43:43,263 --> 00:43:45,003
Why do you seek to kill me?”

566
00:43:45,703 --> 00:43:48,303
The multitude answered, “You have a demon!

567
00:43:48,343 --> 00:43:50,043
Who seeks to kill you?”

568
00:43:51,123 --> 00:43:56,463
Jesus answered them, “I did one work and
you all marvel because of it.

569
00:43:56,606 --> 00:44:03,706
Moses has given you circumcision (not that
it is of Moses, but of the fathers), and

570
00:44:03,746 --> 00:44:05,886
on the Sabbath you circumcise a boy.

571
00:44:06,846 --> 00:44:13,006
If a boy receives circumcision on the Sabbath,
that the law of Moses may not be broken,

572
00:44:13,906 --> 00:44:18,526
are you angry with me because I made a man
completely healthy on the Sabbath?

573
00:44:18,566 --> 00:44:24,606
Don’t judge according to appearance, but
judge righteous judgement.”

574
00:44:24,646 --> 00:44:30,546
Therefore some of them of Jerusalem said,
“Isn’t this he whom they seek to kill?

575
00:44:31,386 --> 00:44:35,486
Behold, he speaks openly, and they say
nothing to him.

576
00:44:36,366 --> 00:44:40,586
Can it be that the rulers indeed know that
this is truly the Christ?

577
00:44:41,266 --> 00:44:47,566
However, we know where this man comes from,
but when the Christ comes, no one will know

578
00:44:47,606 --> 00:44:48,706
where he comes from.”

579
00:44:49,506 --> 00:44:55,906
Jesus therefore cried out in the temple,
teaching and saying, “You both know me, and

580
00:44:55,946 --> 00:44:57,006
know where I am from.

581
00:44:57,886 --> 00:45:03,186
I have not come of myself, but he who sent
me is true, whom you don’t know.

582
00:45:03,866 --> 00:45:07,486
I know him, because I am from him, and he
sent me.”

583
00:45:08,186 --> 00:45:14,666
They sought therefore to take him; but no one
laid a hand on him, because his hour had

584
00:45:14,706 --> 00:45:15,606
not yet come.

585
00:45:16,486 --> 00:45:19,466
But of the multitude, many believed in
him.

586
00:45:19,926 --> 00:45:25,906
They said, “When the Christ comes, he won’t
do more signs than those which this man has

587
00:45:25,946 --> 00:45:27,166
done, will he?”

588
00:45:28,126 --> 00:45:33,826
The Pharisees heard the multitude murmuring
these things concerning him, and the chief

589
00:45:33,866 --> 00:45:37,566
priests and the Pharisees sent officers to
arrest him.

590
00:45:38,226 --> 00:45:44,486
Then Jesus said, “I will be with you a
little while longer, then I go to him who sent

591
00:45:44,526 --> 00:45:45,426
me.

592
00:45:45,646 --> 00:45:47,846
You will seek me and won’t find me.

593
00:45:48,506 --> 00:45:50,246
You can’t come where I am.”

594
00:45:51,066 --> 00:45:56,726
The Jews therefore said amongst themselves, “Where
will this man go that we won’t find

595
00:45:56,766 --> 00:45:57,586
him?

596
00:45:57,626 --> 00:46:01,466
Will he go to the Dispersion amongst the
Greeks and teach the Greeks?

597
00:46:02,246 --> 00:46:08,446
What is this word that he said, ‘You will
seek me, and won’t find me;’ and ‘Where I am,

598
00:46:08,486 --> 00:46:09,386
you can’t come’?”

599
00:46:10,146 --> 00:46:16,726
Now on the last and greatest day of
the feast, Jesus stood and cried out, “If anyone

600
00:46:16,766 --> 00:46:19,846
is thirsty, let him come to me and drink!

601
00:46:20,270 --> 00:46:26,770
He who believes in me, as the Scripture
has said, from within him will flow rivers

602
00:46:26,810 --> 00:46:27,930
of living water.”

603
00:46:29,050 --> 00:46:34,610
But he said this about the Spirit, which
those believing in him were to receive.

604
00:46:36,030 --> 00:46:41,550
For the Holy Spirit was not yet given,
because Jesus wasn’t yet glorified.

605
00:46:42,230 --> 00:46:48,270
Many of the multitude therefore, when they
heard these words, said, “This is truly the

606
00:46:48,310 --> 00:46:49,210
prophet.”

607
00:46:49,810 --> 00:46:52,250
Others said, “This is the Christ.”

608
00:46:53,250 --> 00:46:58,250
But some said, “What, does the Christ come
out of Galilee?

609
00:46:58,490 --> 00:47:04,230
Hasn’t the Scripture said that the Christ comes
of the offspring of David, and from Bethlehem,

610
00:47:05,050 --> 00:47:06,490
the village where David was?”

611
00:47:07,750 --> 00:47:11,010
So a division arose in the multitude
because of him.

612
00:47:11,650 --> 00:47:16,250
Some of them would have arrested him, but
no one laid hands on him.

613
00:47:16,850 --> 00:47:22,410
The officers therefore came to the chief
priests and Pharisees; and they said to them,

614
00:47:22,970 --> 00:47:24,330
“Why didn’t you bring him?”

615
00:47:25,250 --> 00:47:29,710
The officers answered, “No man ever spoke
like this man!”

616
00:47:30,850 --> 00:47:36,670
The Pharisees therefore answered them,
“You aren’t also led astray, are you?

617
00:47:37,110 --> 00:47:40,830
Have any of the rulers or any of the
Pharisees believed in him?

618
00:47:41,730 --> 00:47:44,910
But this multitude that doesn’t know the
law is cursed.”

619
00:47:46,430 --> 00:47:52,890
Nicodemus (he who came to him by night,
being one of them) said to them, “Does

620
00:47:52,930 --> 00:48:02,870
our law judge a man unless it first hears
from

621
00:48:02,910 --> 00:48:03,210
him personally and knows what he does?”

622
00:48:03,250 --> 00:48:03,550
They answered him, “Are you also from
Galilee?

623
00:48:03,590 --> 00:48:06,890
Search and see that no prophet has arisen
out of Galilee.”

624
00:48:07,490 --> 00:48:12,430
Everyone went to his own house, John,
chapter eight.

625
00:48:12,470 --> 00:48:14,730
but Jesus went to the Mount of Olives.

626
00:48:15,490 --> 00:48:21,650
Now very early in the morning, he came
again into the temple, and all the people came

627
00:48:21,690 --> 00:48:22,590
to him.

628
00:48:22,950 --> 00:48:24,630
He sat down and taught them.

629
00:48:24,670 --> 00:48:28,730
The scribes and the Pharisees brought a
woman taken in adultery.

630
00:48:29,870 --> 00:48:36,330
Having set her in the middle, they told
him, “Teacher, we found this woman in adultery,

631
00:48:36,370 --> 00:48:38,050
in the very act.

632
00:48:38,710 --> 00:48:43,290
Now in our law, Moses commanded us to
stone such women.

633
00:48:44,170 --> 00:48:45,990
What then do you say about her?”

634
00:48:46,670 --> 00:48:51,910
They said this testing him, that they
might have something to accuse him of.

635
00:48:52,249 --> 00:48:56,429
But Jesus stooped down and wrote on the
ground with his finger.

636
00:48:57,469 --> 00:49:03,809
But when they continued asking him, he looked
up and said to them, “He who is without

637
00:49:03,849 --> 00:49:08,089
sin amongst you, let him throw the first
stone at her.”

638
00:49:09,229 --> 00:49:13,069
Again he stooped down and wrote on the
ground with his finger.

639
00:49:13,689 --> 00:49:21,089
They, when they heard it, being convicted by
their conscience, went out one by one, beginning

640
00:49:21,129 --> 00:49:23,909
from the oldest, even to the last.

641
00:49:24,949 --> 00:49:29,289
Jesus was left alone with the woman where
she was, in the middle.

642
00:49:29,769 --> 00:49:36,329
Jesus, standing up, saw her and said,
“Woman, where are your accusers?

643
00:49:36,849 --> 00:49:38,369
Did no one condemn you?”

644
00:49:38,949 --> 00:49:40,749
She said, “No one, Lord.”

645
00:49:41,349 --> 00:49:44,389
Jesus said, “Neither do I condemn you.

646
00:49:45,009 --> 00:49:45,909
Go your way.

647
00:49:46,489 --> 00:49:48,569
From now on, sin no more.”

648
00:49:49,589 --> 00:49:55,709
Again, therefore, Jesus spoke to them,
saying, “I am the light of the world.

649
00:49:56,569 --> 00:50:02,029
He who follows me will not walk in
the darkness, but will have the light of life.”

650
00:50:02,849 --> 00:50:07,029
The Pharisees therefore said to him, “You
testify about yourself.

651
00:50:08,089 --> 00:50:09,669
Your testimony is not valid.”

652
00:50:10,869 --> 00:50:18,169
Jesus answered them, “Even if I testify
about myself, my testimony is true, for

653
00:50:18,209 --> 00:50:24,289
I know where I came from, and where I
am going; but you don’t know where I came from,

654
00:50:24,329 --> 00:50:25,869
or where I am going.

655
00:50:26,549 --> 00:50:28,349
You judge according to the flesh.

656
00:50:28,949 --> 00:50:30,089
I judge no one.

657
00:50:30,769 --> 00:50:37,269
Even if I do judge, my judgement is true,
for I am not alone, but I am with the

658
00:50:37,309 --> 00:50:38,449
Father who sent me.

659
00:50:39,209 --> 00:50:44,169
It’s also written in your law that the
testimony of two people is valid.

660
00:50:44,789 --> 00:50:50,989
I am one who testifies about myself, and
the Father who sent me testifies about me.”

661
00:50:51,869 --> 00:50:55,629
They said therefore to him, “Where is your
Father?”

662
00:50:56,569 --> 00:51:00,609
Jesus answered, “You know neither me nor
my Father.

663
00:51:01,169 --> 00:51:04,309
If you knew me, you would know my Father
also.”

664
00:51:05,209 --> 00:51:09,349
Jesus spoke these words in the treasury,
as he taught in the temple.

665
00:51:10,429 --> 00:51:14,649
Yet no one arrested him, because his hour
had not yet come.

666
00:51:15,429 --> 00:51:22,069
Jesus said therefore again to them, “I am
going away, and you will seek me, and you

667
00:51:22,109 --> 00:51:23,289
will die in your sins.

668
00:51:24,109 --> 00:51:26,029
Where I go, you can’t come.”

669
00:51:26,362 --> 00:51:32,982
The Jews therefore said, “Will he kill himself,
because he says, ‘Where I am going, you

670
00:51:33,022 --> 00:51:33,922
can’t come’?”

671
00:51:34,622 --> 00:51:37,282
He said to them, “You are from beneath.

672
00:51:38,102 --> 00:51:39,242
I am from above.

673
00:51:39,882 --> 00:51:41,322
You are of this world.

674
00:51:42,082 --> 00:51:43,542
I am not of this world.

675
00:51:44,502 --> 00:51:50,122
I said therefore to you that you will die
in your sins; for unless you believe that I

676
00:51:50,162 --> 00:51:52,622
am he, you will die in your sins.”

677
00:51:53,762 --> 00:51:56,422
They said therefore to him, “Who are you?”

678
00:51:57,142 --> 00:52:01,602
Jesus said to them, “Just what I have been
saying to you from the beginning.

679
00:52:02,462 --> 00:52:05,762
I have many things to speak and to judge
concerning you.

680
00:52:06,542 --> 00:52:13,122
However, he who sent me is true; and the
things which I heard from him, these I say

681
00:52:13,162 --> 00:52:14,062
to the world.”

682
00:52:14,482 --> 00:52:17,762
They didn’t understand that he spoke to
them about the Father.

683
00:52:18,382 --> 00:52:24,322
Jesus therefore said to them, “When you have
lifted up the Son of Man, then you will

684
00:52:24,362 --> 00:52:31,002
know that I am he, and I do nothing of
myself, but as my Father taught me, I say

685
00:52:31,042 --> 00:52:31,942
these things.

686
00:52:32,662 --> 00:52:34,442
He who sent me is with me.

687
00:52:34,702 --> 00:52:40,282
The Father hasn’t left me alone, for I
always do the things that are pleasing to him.”

688
00:52:40,922 --> 00:52:43,922
As he spoke these things, many believed in
him.

689
00:52:44,722 --> 00:52:51,062
Jesus therefore said to those Jews who had
believed him, “If you remain in my word, then

690
00:52:51,102 --> 00:52:52,442
you are truly my disciples.

691
00:52:53,502 --> 00:52:56,762
You will know the truth, and the truth
will make you free.”

692
00:52:57,402 --> 00:53:03,502
They answered him, “We are Abraham’s offspring,
and have never been in bondage to anyone.

693
00:53:04,502 --> 00:53:06,982
How do you say, ‘You will be made free’?”

694
00:53:08,162 --> 00:53:14,722
Jesus answered them, “Most certainly I
tell you, everyone who commits sin is the

695
00:53:14,762 --> 00:53:15,982
bondservant of sin.

696
00:53:16,962 --> 00:53:19,422
A bondservant doesn’t live in the house
forever.

697
00:53:20,142 --> 00:53:21,742
A son remains forever.

698
00:53:22,902 --> 00:53:26,822
If therefore the Son makes you free, you
will be free indeed.

699
00:53:27,982 --> 00:53:33,842
I know that you are Abraham’s offspring, yet
you seek to kill me, because my word finds

700
00:53:33,882 --> 00:53:35,042
no place in you.

701
00:53:35,762 --> 00:53:41,222
I say the things which I have seen with
my Father; and you also do the things which you

702
00:53:41,262 --> 00:53:42,642
have seen with your father.”

703
00:53:42,682 --> 00:53:46,422
They answered him, “Our father is
Abraham.”

704
00:53:47,065 --> 00:53:52,825
Jesus said to them, “If you were Abraham’s
children, you would do the works of Abraham.

705
00:53:53,725 --> 00:53:59,865
But now you seek to kill me, a man who has
told you the truth which I heard from God.

706
00:54:01,205 --> 00:54:02,825
Abraham didn’t do this.

707
00:54:03,645 --> 00:54:05,285
You do the works of your father.”

708
00:54:05,605 --> 00:54:09,665
They said to him, “We were not born of
sexual immorality.

709
00:54:10,385 --> 00:54:11,825
We have one Father, God.”

710
00:54:12,365 --> 00:54:18,885
Therefore Jesus said to them, “If God were
your father, you would love me, for I came

711
00:54:18,925 --> 00:54:20,825
out and have come from God.

712
00:54:21,505 --> 00:54:24,885
For I haven’t come of myself, but he sent
me.

713
00:54:25,805 --> 00:54:28,025
Why don’t you understand my speech?

714
00:54:28,865 --> 00:54:30,485
Because you can’t hear my word.

715
00:54:31,245 --> 00:54:36,185
You are of your father the devil, and you
want to do the desires of your father.

716
00:54:36,905 --> 00:54:42,605
He was a murderer from the beginning, and
doesn’t stand in the truth, because there is

717
00:54:42,645 --> 00:54:43,605
no truth in him.

718
00:54:43,645 --> 00:54:50,345
When he speaks a lie, he speaks on his own;
for he is a liar, and the father of lies.

719
00:54:51,105 --> 00:54:53,985
But because I tell the truth, you don’t
believe me.

720
00:54:54,925 --> 00:54:56,785
Which of you convicts me of sin?

721
00:54:57,705 --> 00:55:00,945
If I tell the truth, why do you not
believe me?

722
00:55:01,965 --> 00:55:04,545
He who is of God hears the words of God.

723
00:55:05,525 --> 00:55:08,865
For this cause you don’t hear, because you
are not of God.”

724
00:55:09,445 --> 00:55:15,605
Then the Jews answered him, “Don’t we say well
that you are a Samaritan, and have a demon?”

725
00:55:16,605 --> 00:55:22,645
Jesus answered, “I don’t have a demon, but
I honour my Father and you dishonour me.

726
00:55:23,185 --> 00:55:25,225
But I don’t seek my own glory.

727
00:55:26,225 --> 00:55:28,065
There is one who seeks and judges.

728
00:55:28,885 --> 00:55:34,585
Most certainly, I tell you, if a person
keeps my word, he will never see death.”

729
00:55:35,525 --> 00:55:39,745
Then the Jews said to him, “Now we know
that you have a demon.

730
00:55:40,805 --> 00:55:47,345
Abraham died, as did the prophets; and you
say, ‘If a man keeps my word, he will

731
00:55:47,385 --> 00:55:48,585
never taste of death.’

732
00:55:49,205 --> 00:55:51,845
Are you greater than our father Abraham,
who died?

733
00:55:52,705 --> 00:55:53,605
The prophets died.

734
00:55:54,685 --> 00:55:56,425
Who do you make yourself out to be?”

735
00:55:57,245 --> 00:56:02,225
Jesus answered, “If I glorify myself, my
glory is nothing.

736
00:56:02,905 --> 00:56:07,565
It is my Father who glorifies me, of whom
you say that he is our God.

737
00:56:08,445 --> 00:56:10,865
You have not known him, but I know him.

738
00:56:11,385 --> 00:56:15,785
If I said, ‘I don’t know him,’ I would be
like you, a liar.

739
00:56:16,179 --> 00:56:18,399
But I know him and keep his word.

740
00:56:19,759 --> 00:56:22,799
Your father Abraham rejoiced to see my
day.

741
00:56:23,739 --> 00:56:25,419
He saw it and was glad.”

742
00:56:26,519 --> 00:56:31,319
The Jews therefore said to him, “You are
not yet fifty years old!

743
00:56:32,219 --> 00:56:33,119
Have you seen Abraham?”

744
00:56:33,959 --> 00:56:39,879
Jesus said to them, “Most certainly, I
tell you, before Abraham came into existence,

745
00:56:40,719 --> 00:56:41,619
I AM.”

746
00:56:41,919 --> 00:56:48,319
Therefore they took up stones to throw at
him, but Jesus was hid himself and went out

747
00:56:48,359 --> 00:56:53,319
of the temple, having gone through the
middle of them, and so passed by.

748
00:56:54,319 --> 00:56:57,059
John, chapter nine.

749
00:56:57,099 --> 00:57:00,739
As he passed by, he saw a man blind from
birth.

750
00:57:01,499 --> 00:57:08,439
His disciples asked him, “Rabbi, who
sinned, this man or his parents, that

751
00:57:08,479 --> 00:57:09,379
he was born blind?”

752
00:57:10,639 --> 00:57:17,239
Jesus answered, “This man didn’t sin, nor
did his parents, but that the works of

753
00:57:17,279 --> 00:57:19,179
God might be revealed in him.

754
00:57:20,159 --> 00:57:23,939
I must work the works of him who sent me
while it is day.

755
00:57:24,679 --> 00:57:27,619
The night is coming, when no one can work.

756
00:57:28,599 --> 00:57:32,119
While I am in the world, I am the light of
the world.”

757
00:57:33,019 --> 00:57:39,659
When he had said this, he spat on the
ground, made mud with the saliva, anointed

758
00:57:39,699 --> 00:57:47,059
the blind man’s eyes with the mud, and said
to him, “Go, wash in the pool of Siloam”

759
00:57:47,099 --> 00:57:48,179
(which means “Sent”).

760
00:57:48,879 --> 00:57:52,539
So he went away, washed, and came back
seeing.

761
00:57:53,359 --> 00:57:59,279
Therefore the neighbours and those who saw
that he was blind before said, “Isn’t this

762
00:57:59,319 --> 00:58:00,899
he who sat and begged?”

763
00:58:01,919 --> 00:58:03,859
Others were saying, “It is he.”

764
00:58:04,519 --> 00:58:07,359
Still others were saying, “He looks like
him.”

765
00:58:07,939 --> 00:58:09,659
He said, “I am he.”

766
00:58:10,259 --> 00:58:14,139
They therefore were asking him, “How were
your eyes opened?”

767
00:58:15,119 --> 00:58:21,759
He answered, “A man called Jesus made mud,
anointed my eyes, and said

768
00:58:21,799 --> 00:58:25,119
to me, ‘Go to the pool of Siloam and
wash.’

769
00:58:26,099 --> 00:58:29,559
So I went away and washed, and I received
sight.”

770
00:58:30,539 --> 00:58:32,879
Then they asked him, “Where is he?”

771
00:58:33,559 --> 00:58:35,259
He said, “I don’t know.”

772
00:58:35,999 --> 00:58:38,939
They brought him who had been blind to the
Pharisees.

773
00:58:39,779 --> 00:58:43,859
It was a Sabbath when Jesus made the mud
and opened his eyes.

774
00:58:44,939 --> 00:58:49,659
Again therefore the Pharisees also asked
him how he received his sight.

775
00:58:50,179 --> 00:58:55,199
He said to them, “He put mud on my eyes, I
washed, and I see.”

776
00:58:55,589 --> 00:59:02,049
Some therefore of the Pharisees said, “This
man is not from God, because he doesn’t

777
00:59:02,089 --> 00:59:02,989
keep the Sabbath.”

778
00:59:04,069 --> 00:59:08,509
Others said, “How can a man who is a
sinner do such signs?”

779
00:59:09,369 --> 00:59:11,529
So there was division amongst them.

780
00:59:12,129 --> 00:59:17,629
Therefore they asked the blind man again, “What
do you say about him, because he opened

781
00:59:17,669 --> 00:59:18,569
your eyes?”

782
00:59:19,329 --> 00:59:21,169
He said, “He is a prophet.”

783
00:59:22,089 --> 00:59:27,389
The Jews therefore didn’t believe concerning him,
that he had been blind and had received

784
00:59:27,429 --> 00:59:33,309
his sight, until they called the parents of
him who had received his sight, and asked

785
00:59:33,349 --> 00:59:37,249
them, “Is this your son, whom you say was
born blind?

786
00:59:38,109 --> 00:59:39,569
How then does he now see?”

787
00:59:40,149 --> 00:59:46,009
His parents answered them, “We know that this
is our son, and that he was born blind;

788
00:59:46,589 --> 00:59:51,909
but how he now sees, we don’t know; or who
opened his eyes, we don’t know.

789
00:59:51,949 --> 00:59:53,489
He is of age.

790
00:59:54,169 --> 00:59:55,069
Ask him.

791
00:59:55,449 --> 00:59:56,649
He will speak for himself.”

792
00:59:57,949 --> 01:00:03,089
His parents said these things because they
feared the Jews; for the Jews had already

793
01:00:03,129 --> 01:00:08,789
agreed that if any man would confess him as
Christ, he would be put out of the synagogue.

794
01:00:09,869 --> 01:00:12,889
Therefore his parents said, “He is of age.

795
01:00:13,469 --> 01:00:14,309
Ask him.”

796
01:00:14,349 --> 01:00:20,689
So they called the man who was blind a
second time, and said to him, “Give glory to God.

797
01:00:20,729 --> 01:00:23,369
We know that this man is a sinner.”

798
01:00:24,009 --> 01:00:27,609
He therefore answered, “I don’t know if he
is a sinner.

799
01:00:28,469 --> 01:00:33,229
One thing I do know: that though I was
blind, now I see.”

800
01:00:34,249 --> 01:00:37,589
They said to him again, “What did he do to
you?

801
01:00:38,269 --> 01:00:39,789
How did he open your eyes?”

802
01:00:40,649 --> 01:00:44,849
He answered them, “I told you already, and
you didn’t listen.

803
01:00:45,429 --> 01:00:47,089
Why do you want to hear it again?

804
01:00:47,789 --> 01:00:51,169
You don’t also want to become his
disciples, do you?”

805
01:00:51,909 --> 01:00:57,829
They insulted him and said, “You are his
disciple, but we are disciples of Moses.

806
01:00:58,809 --> 01:01:00,889
We know that God has spoken to Moses.

807
01:01:01,369 --> 01:01:04,869
But as for this man, we don’t know where
he comes from.”

808
01:01:05,549 --> 01:01:07,949
The man answered them, “How amazing!

809
01:01:09,189 --> 01:01:12,349
You don’t know where he comes from, yet he
opened my eyes.

810
01:01:12,989 --> 01:01:19,049
We know that God doesn’t listen to sinners,
but if anyone is a worshipper of God and

811
01:01:19,089 --> 01:01:21,489
does his will, he listens to him.

812
01:01:21,841 --> 01:01:27,401
Since the world began it has never been
heard of that anyone opened the eyes of someone

813
01:01:27,441 --> 01:01:28,341
born blind.

814
01:01:29,081 --> 01:01:32,881
If this man were not from God, he could do
nothing.”

815
01:01:33,561 --> 01:01:39,381
They answered him, “You were altogether
born in sins, and do you teach us?”

816
01:01:40,041 --> 01:01:41,521
Then they threw him out.

817
01:01:42,341 --> 01:01:48,721
Jesus heard that they had thrown him out,
and finding him, he said, “Do you believe in

818
01:01:48,761 --> 01:01:49,661
the Son of God?”

819
01:01:50,401 --> 01:01:54,621
He answered, “Who is he, Lord, that I may
believe in him?”

820
01:01:55,021 --> 01:02:00,361
Jesus said to him, “You have both seen
him, and it is he who speaks with you.”

821
01:02:01,281 --> 01:02:03,841
He said, “Lord, I believe!”

822
01:02:04,461 --> 01:02:05,721
and he worshipped him.

823
01:02:06,981 --> 01:02:12,981
Jesus said, “I came into this world for
judgement, that those who don’t see may see;

824
01:02:13,461 --> 01:02:15,941
and that those who see may become blind.”

825
01:02:16,861 --> 01:02:22,941
Those of the Pharisees who were with him
heard these things, and said to him, “Are we

826
01:02:22,981 --> 01:02:23,881
also blind?”

827
01:02:24,561 --> 01:02:31,301
Jesus said to them, “If you were blind, you
would have no sin; but now you say, ‘We

828
01:02:31,341 --> 01:02:32,241
see.’

829
01:02:33,021 --> 01:02:34,241
Therefore your sin remains.

830
01:02:35,221 --> 01:02:37,181
John, chapter ten.

831
01:02:37,221 --> 01:02:43,641
“Most certainly, I tell you, one who doesn’t
enter by the door into the sheep fold, but

832
01:02:43,681 --> 01:02:47,521
climbs up some other way, is a thief and a
robber.

833
01:02:48,181 --> 01:02:52,081
But one who enters in by the door is the
shepherd of the sheep.

834
01:02:52,961 --> 01:02:57,581
The gatekeeper opens the gate for him, and
the sheep listen to his voice.

835
01:02:58,461 --> 01:03:02,021
He calls his own sheep by name and leads
them out.

836
01:03:02,461 --> 01:03:07,841
Whenever he brings out his own sheep, he
goes before them; and the sheep follow him,

837
01:03:08,221 --> 01:03:09,421
for they know his voice.

838
01:03:09,461 --> 01:03:15,821
They will by no means follow a stranger,
but will flee from him; for they don’t know

839
01:03:15,861 --> 01:03:16,921
the voice of strangers.”

840
01:03:18,301 --> 01:03:23,441
Jesus spoke this parable to them, but
they didn’t understand what he was telling them.

841
01:03:24,341 --> 01:03:30,621
Jesus therefore said to them again, “Most certainly,
I tell you, I am the sheep’s door.

842
01:03:31,241 --> 01:03:36,861
All who came before me are thieves and
robbers, but the sheep didn’t listen to them.

843
01:03:37,601 --> 01:03:38,501
I am the door.

844
01:03:39,341 --> 01:03:45,921
If anyone enters in by me, he will be saved,
and will go in and go out and will find

845
01:03:45,961 --> 01:03:46,861
pasture.

846
01:03:47,621 --> 01:03:50,941
The thief only comes to steal, kill, and
destroy.

847
01:03:51,419 --> 01:03:55,079
I came that they may have life, and may
have it abundantly.

848
01:03:56,139 --> 01:03:57,199
“I am the good shepherd.

849
01:03:58,159 --> 01:04:01,219
The good shepherd lays down his life for
the sheep.

850
01:04:01,879 --> 01:04:08,399
He who is a hired hand, and not
a shepherd, who doesn’t own the sheep, sees the

851
01:04:08,439 --> 01:04:11,599
wolf coming, leaves the sheep, and flees.

852
01:04:12,099 --> 01:04:14,599
The wolf snatches the sheep and scatters
them.

853
01:04:15,519 --> 01:04:20,599
The hired hand flees because he is a hired
hand and doesn’t care for the sheep.

854
01:04:21,939 --> 01:04:22,839
I am the good shepherd.

855
01:04:23,659 --> 01:04:30,199
I know my own, and I’m known by my own;
even as the Father knows me, and I

856
01:04:30,239 --> 01:04:31,139
know the Father.

857
01:04:31,859 --> 01:04:34,279
I lay down my life for the sheep.

858
01:04:34,859 --> 01:04:37,379
I have other sheep which are not of this
fold.

859
01:04:38,279 --> 01:04:41,739
I must bring them also, and they will hear
my voice.

860
01:04:42,539 --> 01:04:45,279
They will become one flock with one
shepherd.

861
01:04:46,299 --> 01:04:52,119
Therefore the Father loves me, because I lay
down my life, that I may take it again.

862
01:04:52,619 --> 01:04:56,479
No one takes it away from me, but I lay it
down by myself.

863
01:04:57,279 --> 01:05:01,779
I have power to lay it down, and I have
power to take it again.

864
01:05:02,899 --> 01:05:05,459
I received this commandment from my
Father.”

865
01:05:06,359 --> 01:05:10,879
Therefore a division arose again amongst
the Jews because of these words.

866
01:05:11,739 --> 01:05:15,099
Many of them said, “He has a demon and is
insane!

867
01:05:16,299 --> 01:05:17,499
Why do you listen to him?”

868
01:05:18,099 --> 01:05:22,399
Others said, “These are not the sayings of
one possessed by a demon.

869
01:05:23,279 --> 01:05:27,679
It isn’t possible for a demon to open the
eyes of the blind, is it?”

870
01:05:28,499 --> 01:05:31,119
It was the Feast of the Dedication at
Jerusalem.

871
01:05:32,299 --> 01:05:37,159
It was winter, and Jesus was walking in
the temple, in Solomon’s porch.

872
01:05:38,119 --> 01:05:43,739
The Jews therefore came around him and said to
him, “How long will you hold us in suspense?

873
01:05:44,819 --> 01:05:46,979
If you are the Christ, tell us plainly.”

874
01:05:48,079 --> 01:05:52,039
Jesus answered them, “I told you, and you
don’t believe.

875
01:05:53,019 --> 01:05:57,699
The works that I do in my Father’s name,
these testify about me.

876
01:05:58,279 --> 01:06:03,019
But you don’t believe, because you are not
of my sheep, as I told you.

877
01:06:03,819 --> 01:06:07,979
My sheep hear my voice, and I know them,
and they follow me.

878
01:06:08,439 --> 01:06:10,399
I give eternal life to them.

879
01:06:11,039 --> 01:06:15,079
They will never perish, and no one will
snatch them out of my hand.

880
01:06:15,499 --> 01:06:18,639
My Father who has given them to me is
greater than all.

881
01:06:18,964 --> 01:06:22,404
No one is able to snatch them out of my
Father’s hand.

882
01:06:23,384 --> 01:06:25,544
I and the Father are one.”

883
01:06:26,684 --> 01:06:30,164
Therefore the Jews took up stones again to
stone him.

884
01:06:31,084 --> 01:06:36,024
Jesus answered them, “I have shown you
many good works from my Father.

885
01:06:36,964 --> 01:06:39,344
For which of those works do you stone me?”

886
01:06:39,904 --> 01:06:46,264
The Jews answered him, “We don’t stone you
for a good work, but for blasphemy, because

887
01:06:46,304 --> 01:06:49,684
you, being a man, make yourself God.”

888
01:06:50,844 --> 01:06:56,524
Jesus answered them, “Isn’t it written in
your law, ‘I said, you are gods?’

889
01:06:57,304 --> 01:07:03,104
If he called them gods, to whom the word
of God came (and the Scripture can’t be broken),

890
01:07:04,064 --> 01:07:10,164
do you say of him whom the Father
sanctified and sent into the world, ‘You blaspheme,’

891
01:07:10,204 --> 01:07:13,244
because I said, ‘I am the Son of God?’

892
01:07:13,284 --> 01:07:17,844
If I don’t do the works of my Father,
don’t believe me.

893
01:07:18,244 --> 01:07:24,764
But if I do them, though you don’t believe
me, believe the works, that you may know and

894
01:07:24,804 --> 01:07:28,644
believe that the Father is in me, and I in
the Father.”

895
01:07:29,584 --> 01:07:33,664
They sought again to seize him, and he
went out of their hand.

896
01:07:34,224 --> 01:07:39,784
He went away again beyond the Jordan into
the place where John was baptising at first,

897
01:07:40,444 --> 01:07:41,544
and he stayed there.

898
01:07:42,324 --> 01:07:43,544
Many came to him.

899
01:07:44,024 --> 01:07:50,484
They said, “John indeed did no sign, but
everything that John said about this

900
01:07:50,524 --> 01:07:51,464
man is true.”

901
01:07:51,944 --> 01:07:53,384
Many believed in him there.

902
01:07:54,504 --> 01:07:56,624
John, chapter eleven.

903
01:07:56,664 --> 01:08:03,184
Now a certain man was sick, Lazarus from
Bethany, of the village of Mary and her

904
01:08:03,224 --> 01:08:04,124
sister, Martha.

905
01:08:05,104 --> 01:08:10,584
It was that Mary who had anointed the Lord
with ointment and wiped his feet with her

906
01:08:10,624 --> 01:08:13,844
hair, whose brother Lazarus, was sick.

907
01:08:14,544 --> 01:08:21,144
The sisters therefore sent to him, saying,
“Lord, behold, he for whom you have great

908
01:08:21,184 --> 01:08:22,384
affection is sick.”

909
01:08:23,284 --> 01:08:29,364
But when Jesus heard it, he said, “This sickness
is not to death, but for the glory of

910
01:08:29,404 --> 01:08:33,084
God, that God’s Son may be glorified by
it.”

911
01:08:33,464 --> 01:08:37,344
Now Jesus loved Martha, and her sister,
and Lazarus.

912
01:08:38,084 --> 01:08:43,444
When therefore he heard that he was sick, he
stayed two days in the place where he was.

913
01:08:44,544 --> 01:08:49,744
Then after this he said to the disciples,
“Let’s go into Judea again.”

914
01:08:50,136 --> 01:08:56,096
The disciples asked him, “Rabbi, the Jews
were just trying to stone you.

915
01:08:56,676 --> 01:08:58,036
Are you going there again?”

916
01:08:58,916 --> 01:09:02,296
Jesus answered, “Aren’t there twelve hours
of daylight?

917
01:09:03,156 --> 01:09:09,196
If a man walks in the day, he doesn’t
stumble, because he sees the light of this world.

918
01:09:09,916 --> 01:09:15,136
But if a man walks in the night, he
stumbles, because the light isn’t in him.”

919
01:09:15,976 --> 01:09:22,756
He said these things, and after that, he
said to them, “Our friend Lazarus has fallen

920
01:09:22,796 --> 01:09:26,996
asleep, but I am going so that I may awake
him out of sleep.”

921
01:09:27,756 --> 01:09:33,376
The disciples therefore said, “Lord, if he
has fallen asleep, he will recover.”

922
01:09:34,456 --> 01:09:40,256
Now Jesus had spoken of his death, but they
thought that he spoke of taking rest in sleep.

923
01:09:41,316 --> 01:09:45,256
So Jesus said to them plainly then,
“Lazarus is dead.

924
01:09:45,996 --> 01:09:50,856
I am glad for your sakes that I was not
there, so that you may believe.

925
01:09:52,016 --> 01:09:54,516
Nevertheless, let’s go to him.”

926
01:09:55,696 --> 01:10:02,196
Thomas therefore, who is called Didymus,
said to his fellow disciples, “Let’s also

927
01:10:02,236 --> 01:10:04,616
go, that we may die with him.”

928
01:10:05,316 --> 01:10:10,216
So when Jesus came, he found that he had
been in the tomb four days already.

929
01:10:11,516 --> 01:10:16,056
Now Bethany was near Jerusalem, about
fifteen stadia away.

930
01:10:16,896 --> 01:10:22,196
Many of the Jews had joined the women
around Martha and Mary, to console them concerning

931
01:10:22,236 --> 01:10:23,136
their brother.

932
01:10:23,776 --> 01:10:29,556
Then when Martha heard that Jesus was coming,
she went and met him, but Mary stayed in

933
01:10:29,596 --> 01:10:30,496
the house.

934
01:10:31,176 --> 01:10:37,336
Therefore Martha said to Jesus, “Lord, if
you would have been here, my brother wouldn’t

935
01:10:37,376 --> 01:10:38,276
have died.

936
01:10:38,896 --> 01:10:43,556
Even now I know that whatever you ask of
God, God will give you.”

937
01:10:44,196 --> 01:10:47,276
Jesus said to her, “Your brother will rise
again.”

938
01:10:48,356 --> 01:10:53,956
Martha said to him, “I know that he will
rise again in the resurrection at the last day.”

939
01:10:55,036 --> 01:10:58,696
Jesus said to her, “I am the resurrection
and the life.

940
01:10:59,496 --> 01:11:02,996
He who believes in me will still live,
even if he dies.

941
01:11:03,796 --> 01:11:06,836
Whoever lives and believes in me will
never die.

942
01:11:07,856 --> 01:11:08,776
Do you believe this?”

943
01:11:09,556 --> 01:11:11,376
She said to him, “Yes, Lord.

944
01:11:11,956 --> 01:11:18,596
I have come to believe that you are the
Christ, God’s Son, he who comes into the world.”

945
01:11:18,953 --> 01:11:24,693
When she had said this, she went away and
called Mary, her sister, secretly, saying,

946
01:11:25,653 --> 01:11:27,893
“The Teacher is here and is calling you.”

947
01:11:28,853 --> 01:11:32,713
When she heard this, she arose quickly and
went to him.

948
01:11:33,853 --> 01:11:39,513
Now Jesus had not yet come into the village,
but was in the place where Martha met him.

949
01:11:40,093 --> 01:11:45,213
Then the Jews who were with her in the
house and were consoling her, when they saw Mary,

950
01:11:45,253 --> 01:11:51,813
that she rose up quickly and went out,
followed her, saying, “She is going to the

951
01:11:51,853 --> 01:11:53,113
tomb to weep there.”

952
01:11:53,713 --> 01:12:00,233
Therefore when Mary came to where Jesus was and
saw him, she fell down at his feet, saying

953
01:12:00,273 --> 01:12:05,653
to him, “Lord, if you would have been
here, my brother wouldn’t have died.”

954
01:12:06,193 --> 01:12:12,553
When Jesus therefore saw her weeping, and the
Jews weeping who came with her, he groaned

955
01:12:12,593 --> 01:12:17,173
in the spirit and was troubled, and said,
“Where have you laid him?”

956
01:12:18,053 --> 01:12:20,873
They told him, “Lord, come and see.”

957
01:12:21,853 --> 01:12:23,013
Jesus wept.

958
01:12:23,293 --> 01:12:27,593
The Jews therefore said, “See how much
affection he had for him!”

959
01:12:28,173 --> 01:12:33,973
Some of them said, “Couldn’t this man, who
opened the eyes of him who was blind, have

960
01:12:34,013 --> 01:12:35,953
also kept this man from dying?”

961
01:12:36,973 --> 01:12:41,393
Jesus therefore, again groaning in
himself, came to the tomb.

962
01:12:42,313 --> 01:12:45,953
Now it was a cave, and a stone lay against
it.

963
01:12:46,673 --> 01:12:48,953
Jesus said, “Take away the stone.”

964
01:12:49,793 --> 01:12:56,553
Martha, the sister of him who was dead,
said to him, “Lord, by this time there

965
01:12:56,593 --> 01:12:59,773
is a stench, for he has been dead four
days.”

966
01:13:01,073 --> 01:13:06,893
Jesus said to her, “Didn’t I tell you
that if you believed, you would see God’s glory?”

967
01:13:07,473 --> 01:13:11,433
So they took away the stone from the place
where the dead man was lying.

968
01:13:12,473 --> 01:13:18,353
Jesus lifted up his eyes and said, “Father,
I thank you that you listened to me.

969
01:13:18,833 --> 01:13:26,613
I know that you

970
01:13:26,653 --> 01:13:26,953
always listen to me, but because of the
multitude standing around I said this, that they

971
01:13:26,993 --> 01:13:27,953
may believe that you sent me.”

972
01:13:28,433 --> 01:13:33,873
When he had said this, he cried with a
loud voice, “Lazarus, come out!”

973
01:13:34,953 --> 01:13:40,813
He who was dead came out, bound hand
and foot with wrappings, and his face was wrapped

974
01:13:40,853 --> 01:13:41,973
around with a cloth.

975
01:13:43,093 --> 01:13:46,553
Jesus said to them, “Free him, and let him
go.”

976
01:13:46,906 --> 01:13:53,166
Therefore many of the Jews who came to
Mary and saw what Jesus did believed in him.

977
01:13:54,146 --> 01:13:59,326
But some of them went away to the
Pharisees and told them the things which Jesus had

978
01:13:59,366 --> 01:14:00,266
done.

979
01:14:00,466 --> 01:14:06,706
The chief priests therefore and the Pharisees
gathered a council, and said, “What are

980
01:14:06,746 --> 01:14:07,646
we doing?

981
01:14:07,986 --> 01:14:09,506
For this man does many signs.

982
01:14:10,726 --> 01:14:16,566
If we leave him alone like this, everyone
will believe in him, and the Romans will come

983
01:14:16,606 --> 01:14:19,566
and take away both our place and our
nation.”

984
01:14:20,146 --> 01:14:26,506
But a certain one of them, Caiaphas, being
high priest that year, said to them, “You

985
01:14:26,546 --> 01:14:32,526
know nothing at all, nor do you consider
that it is advantageous for us that one man

986
01:14:32,566 --> 01:14:36,466
should die for the people, and that the
whole nation not perish.”

987
01:14:37,306 --> 01:14:43,766
Now he didn’t say this of himself, but
being high priest that year, he prophesied that

988
01:14:43,806 --> 01:14:50,166
Jesus would die for the nation, and not for
the nation only, but that he might also gather

989
01:14:50,206 --> 01:14:54,466
together into one the children of God who
are scattered abroad.

990
01:14:55,306 --> 01:14:59,526
So from that day forward they took counsel
that they might put him to death.

991
01:15:00,586 --> 01:15:06,826
Jesus therefore walked no more openly amongst
the Jews, but departed from there into

992
01:15:06,866 --> 01:15:11,446
the country near the wilderness, to a city
called Ephraim.

993
01:15:11,486 --> 01:15:13,266
He stayed there with his disciples.

994
01:15:14,006 --> 01:15:16,546
Now the Passover of the Jews was at hand.

995
01:15:17,186 --> 01:15:22,106
Many went up from the country to Jerusalem
before the Passover, to purify themselves.

996
01:15:23,426 --> 01:15:29,326
Then they sought for Jesus and spoke with
one another as they stood in the temple, “What

997
01:15:29,366 --> 01:15:32,466
do you think—that he isn’t coming to the
feast at all?”

998
01:15:33,066 --> 01:15:38,346
Now the chief priests and the Pharisees had
commanded that if anyone knew where he was,

999
01:15:38,826 --> 01:15:41,406
he should report it, that they might seize
him.

1000
01:15:42,386 --> 01:15:44,246
John, chapter twelve.

1001
01:15:44,286 --> 01:15:51,186
Then, six days before the Passover, Jesus
came to Bethany, where Lazarus was, who

1002
01:15:51,226 --> 01:15:53,846
had been dead, whom he raised from the
dead.

1003
01:15:54,386 --> 01:15:55,986
So they made him a supper there.

1004
01:15:57,006 --> 01:16:02,066
Martha served, but Lazarus was one of
those who sat at the table with him.

1005
01:16:02,331 --> 01:16:09,011
Therefore Mary took a pound of ointment of
pure nard, very precious, and anointed

1006
01:16:09,051 --> 01:16:12,531
Jesus’s feet and wiped his feet with her
hair.

1007
01:16:13,531 --> 01:16:16,851
The house was filled with the fragrance of
the ointment.

1008
01:16:17,531 --> 01:16:25,211
Then Judas Iscariot, Simon’s son, one of
his disciples, who would betray him, said, “Why

1009
01:16:25,251 --> 01:16:30,231
wasn’t this ointment sold for three
hundred denarii and given to the poor?”

1010
01:16:30,791 --> 01:16:36,991
Now he said this, not because he cared for
the poor, but because he was a thief, and

1011
01:16:37,031 --> 01:16:40,711
having the money box, used to steal what
was put into it.

1012
01:16:41,491 --> 01:16:43,831
But Jesus said, “Leave her alone.

1013
01:16:44,711 --> 01:16:46,891
She has kept this for the day of my
burial.

1014
01:16:47,971 --> 01:16:52,151
For you always have the poor with you, but
you don’t always have me.”

1015
01:16:52,731 --> 01:16:59,251
A large crowd therefore of the Jews learnt
that he was there; and they came, not for

1016
01:16:59,291 --> 01:17:05,851
Jesus’ sake only, but that they might see
Lazarus also, whom he had raised from the dead.

1017
01:17:06,471 --> 01:17:12,511
But the chief priests conspired to put Lazarus
to death also, because on account of him

1018
01:17:12,551 --> 01:17:16,331
many of the Jews went away and believed in
Jesus.

1019
01:17:17,511 --> 01:17:21,071
On the next day a great multitude had come
to the feast.

1020
01:17:21,711 --> 01:17:26,751
When they heard that Jesus was coming to
Jerusalem, they took the branches of the palm

1021
01:17:26,791 --> 01:17:31,131
trees and went out to meet him, and cried
out, “Hosanna!

1022
01:17:31,171 --> 01:17:36,451
Blessed is he who comes in the name of the
Lord, the King of Israel!”

1023
01:17:37,131 --> 01:17:40,931
Jesus, having found a young donkey, sat on
it.

1024
01:17:41,411 --> 01:17:45,211
As it is written, “Don’t be afraid,
daughter of Zion.

1025
01:17:46,011 --> 01:17:50,271
Behold, your King comes, sitting on a
donkey’s colt.”

1026
01:17:50,731 --> 01:17:56,391
His disciples didn’t understand these things
at first, but when Jesus was glorified,

1027
01:17:57,031 --> 01:18:01,651
then they remembered that these things were
written about him, and that they had done

1028
01:18:01,691 --> 01:18:02,791
these things to him.

1029
01:18:03,331 --> 01:18:08,611
The multitude therefore that was with him
when he called Lazarus out of the tomb and

1030
01:18:08,651 --> 01:18:12,071
raised him from the dead was testifying
about it.

1031
01:18:12,871 --> 01:18:18,531
For this cause also the multitude went and
met him, because they heard that he had done

1032
01:18:18,571 --> 01:18:19,471
this sign.

1033
01:18:19,851 --> 01:18:25,531
The Pharisees therefore said amongst
themselves, “See how you accomplish nothing.

1034
01:18:25,914 --> 01:18:28,954
Behold, the world has gone after him.”

1035
01:18:29,874 --> 01:18:34,414
Now there were certain Greeks amongst
those who went up to worship at the feast.

1036
01:18:35,454 --> 01:18:41,974
Therefore, these came to Philip, who was
from Bethsaida of Galilee, and asked him,

1037
01:18:42,194 --> 01:18:45,514
saying, “Sir, we want to see Jesus.”

1038
01:18:46,454 --> 01:18:53,094
Philip came and told Andrew, and in turn,
Andrew came with Philip, and they told Jesus.

1039
01:18:54,114 --> 01:18:59,454
Jesus answered them, “The time has come
for the Son of Man to be glorified.

1040
01:19:00,074 --> 01:19:06,514
Most certainly I tell you, unless a grain
of wheat falls into the earth and dies, it

1041
01:19:06,554 --> 01:19:08,074
remains by itself alone.

1042
01:19:08,834 --> 01:19:11,334
But if it dies, it bears much fruit.

1043
01:19:12,414 --> 01:19:14,414
He who loves his life will lose it.

1044
01:19:15,194 --> 01:19:19,414
He who hates his life in this world will
keep it to eternal life.

1045
01:19:20,414 --> 01:19:23,094
If anyone serves me, let him follow me.

1046
01:19:23,814 --> 01:19:26,934
Where I am, there my servant will also be.

1047
01:19:27,734 --> 01:19:30,914
If anyone serves me, the Father will
honour him.

1048
01:19:31,754 --> 01:19:33,114
“Now my soul is troubled.

1049
01:19:33,774 --> 01:19:34,694
What shall I say?

1050
01:19:35,614 --> 01:19:37,574
‘Father, save me from this time?’

1051
01:19:38,594 --> 01:19:40,894
But I came to this time for this cause.

1052
01:19:41,954 --> 01:19:43,734
Father, glorify your name!”

1053
01:19:44,454 --> 01:19:50,714
Then a voice came out of the sky, saying,
“I have both glorified it and will glorify

1054
01:19:50,754 --> 01:19:51,654
it again.”

1055
01:19:51,994 --> 01:19:56,174
Therefore the multitude who stood by and
heard it said that it had thundered.

1056
01:19:56,934 --> 01:19:59,994
Others said, “An angel has spoken to him.”

1057
01:20:00,834 --> 01:20:05,894
Jesus answered, “This voice hasn’t come
for my sake, but for your sakes.

1058
01:20:06,894 --> 01:20:08,694
Now is the judgement of this world.

1059
01:20:09,694 --> 01:20:12,174
Now the prince of this world will be cast
out.

1060
01:20:12,214 --> 01:20:18,094
And I, if I am lifted up from the earth,
will draw all people to myself.”

1061
01:20:19,334 --> 01:20:23,814
But he said this, signifying by what kind
of death he should die.

1062
01:20:25,014 --> 01:20:30,534
The multitude answered him, “We have heard out
of the law that the Christ remains forever.

1063
01:20:31,714 --> 01:20:35,154
How do you say, ‘The Son of Man must be
lifted up?’

1064
01:20:35,634 --> 01:20:37,054
Who is this Son of Man?”

1065
01:20:38,054 --> 01:20:42,854
Jesus therefore said to them, “Yet a
little while the light is with you.

1066
01:20:43,454 --> 01:20:47,914
Walk while you have the light, that
darkness doesn’t overtake you.

1067
01:20:48,734 --> 01:20:52,174
He who walks in the darkness doesn’t know
where he is going.

1068
01:20:52,854 --> 01:20:58,174
While you have the light, believe in the
light, that you may become children of light.”

1069
01:20:58,550 --> 01:21:03,250
Jesus said these things, and he departed
and hid himself from them.

1070
01:21:04,010 --> 01:21:09,750
But though he had done so many signs
before them, yet they didn’t believe in him, that

1071
01:21:09,790 --> 01:21:16,430
the word of Isaiah the prophet might be
fulfilled, which he spoke: “Lord, who has

1072
01:21:16,470 --> 01:21:17,610
believed our report?

1073
01:21:18,410 --> 01:21:20,890
To whom has the arm of the Lord been
revealed?”

1074
01:21:22,130 --> 01:21:27,830
For this cause they couldn’t believe, for
Isaiah said again: “He has blinded their eyes

1075
01:21:27,870 --> 01:21:33,230
and he hardened their heart, lest they
should see with their eyes, and perceive with

1076
01:21:33,270 --> 01:21:36,530
their heart, and would turn, and I would
heal them.”

1077
01:21:37,210 --> 01:21:41,330
Isaiah said these things when he saw his
glory, and spoke of him.

1078
