1288
01:37:27,550 --> 01:37:31,630
They will do these things because they
have not known the Father nor me.

1289
01:37:32,090 --> 01:37:37,610
But I have told you these things so that
when the time comes, you may remember that I

1290
01:37:37,650 --> 01:37:38,730
told you about them.

1291
01:37:39,410 --> 01:37:43,810
I didn’t tell you these things from the
beginning, because I was with you.

1292
01:37:44,190 --> 01:37:50,630
But now I am going to him who sent me,
and none of you asks me, ‘Where are you going?’

1293
01:37:50,670 --> 01:37:55,950
But because I have told you these things,
sorrow has filled your heart.

1294
01:37:56,289 --> 01:38:02,789
Nevertheless I tell you the truth: It is
to your advantage that I go away; for if I

1295
01:38:02,829 --> 01:38:06,009
don’t go away, the Counsellor won’t come
to you.

1296
01:38:06,609 --> 01:38:09,749
But if I go, I will send him to you.

1297
01:38:10,509 --> 01:38:16,769
When he has come, he will convict
the world about sin, about righteousness, and about

1298
01:38:16,809 --> 01:38:23,289
judgement; about sin, because they don’t
believe in me; about righteousness, because

1299
01:38:23,329 --> 01:38:29,669
I am going to my Father, and you won’t see
me any more; about judgement, because the

1300
01:38:29,709 --> 01:38:31,629
prince of this world has been judged.

1301
01:38:32,749 --> 01:38:36,889
“I still have many things to tell you, but
you can’t bear them now.

1302
01:38:37,469 --> 01:38:44,169
However, when he, the Spirit of truth, has
come, he will guide you into all truth, for

1303
01:38:44,209 --> 01:38:48,909
he will not speak from himself; but
whatever he hears, he will speak.

1304
01:38:49,869 --> 01:38:52,209
He will declare to you things that are
coming.

1305
01:38:52,249 --> 01:38:58,069
He will glorify me, for he will take from
what is mine and will declare it to you.

1306
01:38:58,569 --> 01:39:05,049
All things that the Father has are mine; therefore
I said that he takes of mine and will

1307
01:39:05,089 --> 01:39:06,069
declare it to you.

1308
01:39:06,889 --> 01:39:09,949
“A little while, and you will not see me.

1309
01:39:10,689 --> 01:39:13,549
Again a little while, and you will see
me.”

1310
01:39:14,029 --> 01:39:19,569
Some of his disciples therefore said to one
another, “What is this that he says to us,

1311
01:39:20,249 --> 01:39:26,109
‘A little while, and you won’t see me, and
again a little while, and you will see me;’

1312
01:39:26,749 --> 01:39:28,789
and, ‘Because I go to the Father’?”

1313
01:39:29,729 --> 01:39:33,969
They said therefore, “What is this that he
says, ‘A little while’?

1314
01:39:34,549 --> 01:39:36,169
We don’t know what he is saying.”

1315
01:39:37,189 --> 01:39:43,529
Therefore Jesus perceived that they wanted to ask
him, and he said to them, “Do you enquire

1316
01:39:43,569 --> 01:39:49,889
amongst yourselves concerning this, that I said,
‘A little while, and you won’t see me,

1317
01:39:50,569 --> 01:39:53,289
and again a little while, and you will see
me?’

1318
01:39:53,769 --> 01:39:58,549
Most certainly I tell you that you will
weep and lament, but the world will rejoice.

1319
01:39:59,469 --> 01:40:03,249
You will be sorrowful, but your sorrow
will be turned into joy.

1320
01:40:04,209 --> 01:40:09,029
A woman, when she gives birth, has sorrow
because her time has come.

1321
01:40:09,380 --> 01:40:15,180
But when she has delivered the child, she
doesn’t remember the anguish any more, for

1322
01:40:15,220 --> 01:40:18,120
the joy that a human being is born into
the world.

1323
01:40:19,040 --> 01:40:24,980
Therefore you now have sorrow, but I will
see you again, and your heart will rejoice,

1324
01:40:26,100 --> 01:40:28,460
and no one will take your joy away from
you.

1325
01:40:29,020 --> 01:40:31,340
“In that day you will ask me no questions.

1326
01:40:32,500 --> 01:40:38,320
Most certainly I tell you, whatever you may ask
of the Father in my name, he will give

1327
01:40:38,360 --> 01:40:39,260
it to you.

1328
01:40:39,820 --> 01:40:43,060
Until now, you have asked nothing in my
name.

1329
01:40:43,900 --> 01:40:48,160
Ask, and you will receive, that your joy
may be made full.

1330
01:40:48,840 --> 01:40:51,740
“I have spoken these things to you in
figures of speech.

1331
01:40:52,660 --> 01:40:58,060
But the time is coming when I will no
more speak to you in figures of speech, but will

1332
01:40:58,100 --> 01:40:59,960
tell you plainly about the Father.

1333
01:41:00,820 --> 01:41:06,980
In that day you will ask in my name; and I
don’t say to you that I will pray to the Father

1334
01:41:07,020 --> 01:41:13,460
for you, for the Father himself loves you,
because you have loved me, and have believed

1335
01:41:13,500 --> 01:41:15,000
that I came from God.

1336
01:41:15,660 --> 01:41:19,080
I came from the Father and have come into
the world.

1337
01:41:19,780 --> 01:41:22,880
Again, I leave the world and go to the
Father.”

1338
01:41:23,620 --> 01:41:30,160
His disciples said to him, “Behold, now
you are speaking plainly, and using no

1339
01:41:30,200 --> 01:41:31,160
figures of speech.

1340
01:41:31,840 --> 01:41:37,540
Now we know that you know all things, and
don’t need for anyone to question you.

1341
01:41:38,240 --> 01:41:40,840
By this we believe that you came from
God.”

1342
01:41:41,320 --> 01:41:44,180
Jesus answered them, “Do you now believe?

1343
01:41:44,820 --> 01:41:51,460
Behold, the time is coming, yes, and has
now come, that you will be scattered,

1344
01:41:52,140 --> 01:41:55,900
everyone to his own place, and you will
leave me alone.

1345
01:41:56,620 --> 01:42:00,080
Yet I am not alone, because the Father is
with me.

1346
01:42:00,120 --> 01:42:04,060
I have told you these things, that in me
you may have peace.

1347
01:42:04,820 --> 01:42:07,580
In the world you have trouble; but cheer
up!

1348
01:42:08,140 --> 01:42:09,600
I have overcome the world.”

1349
01:42:10,500 --> 01:42:13,300
John, chapter seventeen.

1350
01:42:13,340 --> 01:42:20,040
Jesus said these things, then lifting up his
eyes to heaven, he said, “Father, the time

1351
01:42:20,080 --> 01:42:20,980
has come.

1352
01:42:21,240 --> 01:42:27,260
Glorify your Son, that your Son may also
glorify you; even as you gave him authority

1353
01:42:27,300 --> 01:42:33,200
over all flesh, so he will give eternal
life to all whom you have given him.

1354
01:42:33,524 --> 01:42:40,004
This is eternal life, that they should
know you, the only true God, and him

1355
01:42:40,044 --> 01:42:42,104
whom you sent, Jesus Christ.

1356
01:42:43,304 --> 01:42:45,184
I glorified you on the earth.

1357
01:42:46,084 --> 01:42:49,284
I have accomplished the work which you
have given me to do.

1358
01:42:49,324 --> 01:42:55,864
Now, Father, glorify me with your own self
with the glory which I

1359
01:42:55,904 --> 01:42:57,884
had with you before the world existed.

1360
01:42:58,804 --> 01:43:02,844
“I revealed your name to the people whom
you have given me out of the world.

1361
01:43:03,524 --> 01:43:06,684
They were yours, and you have given them
to me.

1362
01:43:07,464 --> 01:43:08,844
They have kept your word.

1363
01:43:09,804 --> 01:43:15,944
Now they have known that all things whatever
you have given me are from you, for the

1364
01:43:15,984 --> 01:43:21,324
words which you have given me I have given
to them; and they received them, and knew

1365
01:43:21,364 --> 01:43:23,264
for sure that I came from you.

1366
01:43:24,084 --> 01:43:26,104
They have believed that you sent me.

1367
01:43:26,784 --> 01:43:27,844
I pray for them.

1368
01:43:28,244 --> 01:43:33,684
I don’t pray for the world, but for those
whom you have given me, for they are yours.

1369
01:43:34,364 --> 01:43:40,144
All things that are mine are yours, and
yours are mine, and I am glorified in them.

1370
01:43:40,644 --> 01:43:46,184
I am no more in the world, but these are
in the world, and I am coming to you.

1371
01:43:47,244 --> 01:43:53,484
Holy Father, keep them through your name which
you have given me, that they may be one,

1372
01:43:54,024 --> 01:43:55,164
even as we are.

1373
01:43:55,664 --> 01:43:59,284
While I was with them in the world, I kept
them in your name.

1374
01:44:00,144 --> 01:44:02,604
I have kept those whom you have given me.

1375
01:44:03,184 --> 01:44:08,544
None of them is lost except the son
of destruction, that the Scripture might be fulfilled.

1376
01:44:09,664 --> 01:44:15,704
But now I come to you, and I say these
things in the world, that they may have my joy

1377
01:44:15,744 --> 01:44:17,084
made full in themselves.

1378
01:44:18,204 --> 01:44:19,704
I have given them your word.

1379
01:44:20,464 --> 01:44:26,384
The world hated them because they are not of
the world, even as I am not of the world.

1380
01:44:27,324 --> 01:44:32,064
I pray not that you would take them from
the world, but that you would keep them from

1381
01:44:32,104 --> 01:44:33,004
the evil one.

1382
01:44:33,344 --> 01:44:36,824
They are not of the world, even as I am
not of the world.

1383
01:44:37,864 --> 01:44:39,344
Sanctify them in your truth.

1384
01:44:40,164 --> 01:44:41,204
Your word is truth.

1385
01:44:41,944 --> 01:44:46,524
As you sent me into the world, even so I
have sent them into the world.

1386
01:44:47,384 --> 01:44:53,664
For their sakes I sanctify myself, that
they themselves also may be sanctified in truth.

1387
01:44:54,080 --> 01:45:00,200
“Not for these only do I pray, but for
those also who will believe in me through their

1388
01:45:00,240 --> 01:45:07,000
word, that they may all be one; even as
you, Father, are in me, and

1389
01:45:07,040 --> 01:45:13,640
I in you, that they also may be one in us;
that the world may believe that you sent

1390
01:45:13,680 --> 01:45:14,439
me.

1391
01:45:14,479 --> 01:45:21,160
The glory which you have given me, I have
given to them, that they may be one, even as

1392
01:45:21,200 --> 01:45:27,740
we are one, I in them, and you in me, that
they may be perfected into one,

1393
01:45:28,500 --> 01:45:33,840
that the world may know that you sent me
and loved them, even as you loved me.

1394
01:45:34,340 --> 01:45:41,260
Father, I desire that they also whom you
have given me be with me where I am, that

1395
01:45:41,300 --> 01:45:46,640
they may see my glory which you have given
me, for you loved me before the foundation

1396
01:45:46,680 --> 01:45:47,750
of the world.

1397
01:45:48,010 --> 01:45:54,430
Righteous Father, the world hasn’t known you, but
I knew you; and these knew that you

1398
01:45:54,470 --> 01:45:55,370
sent me.

1399
01:45:55,650 --> 01:46:01,490
I made known to them your name, and will
make it known; that the love with which you

1400
01:46:01,530 --> 01:46:05,170
loved me may be in them, and I in them.”

1401
01:46:06,150 --> 01:46:08,890
John, chapter eighteen.

1402
01:46:08,930 --> 01:46:15,370
When Jesus had spoken these words, he went
out with his disciples over the brook Kidron,

1403
01:46:15,410 --> 01:46:19,550
where there was a garden, into which he
and his disciples entered.

1404
01:46:20,750 --> 01:46:27,229
Now Judas, who betrayed him, also knew the
place, for Jesus often met there with his

1405
01:46:27,269 --> 01:46:28,169
disciples.

1406
01:46:28,390 --> 01:46:34,170
Judas then, having taken a detachment of
soldiers and officers from the chief priests

1407
01:46:34,210 --> 01:46:38,970
and the Pharisees, came there with
lanterns, torches, and weapons.

1408
01:46:40,150 --> 01:46:45,810
Jesus therefore, knowing all the things that
were happening to him, went out and said

1409
01:46:45,850 --> 01:46:48,250
to them, “Who are you looking for?”

1410
01:46:48,830 --> 01:46:51,510
They answered him, “Jesus of Nazareth.”

1411
01:46:52,510 --> 01:46:55,110
Jesus said to them, “I am he.”

1412
01:46:56,170 --> 01:47:00,050
Judas also, who betrayed him, was standing
with them.

1413
01:47:01,150 --> 01:47:06,950
When therefore he said to them, “I am he,”
they went backward and fell to the ground.

1414
01:47:08,030 --> 01:47:11,550
Again therefore he asked them, “Who are
you looking for?”

1415
01:47:12,250 --> 01:47:14,630
They said, “Jesus of Nazareth.”

1416
01:47:15,650 --> 01:47:19,110
Jesus answered, “I told you that I am he.

1417
01:47:19,522 --> 01:47:26,282
If therefore you seek me, let these go
their way,” that the word might be fulfilled which

1418
01:47:26,322 --> 01:47:31,382
he spoke, “Of those whom you have given
me, I have lost none.”

1419
01:47:32,702 --> 01:47:39,682
Simon Peter therefore, having a sword, drew
it, struck the high priest’s servant, and

1420
01:47:39,722 --> 01:47:41,002
cut off his right ear.

1421
01:47:41,662 --> 01:47:43,442
The servant’s name was Malchus.

1422
01:47:44,382 --> 01:47:49,022
Jesus therefore said to Peter, “Put the
sword into its sheath.

1423
01:47:49,702 --> 01:47:54,142
The cup which the Father has given me,
shall I not surely drink it?”

1424
01:47:54,582 --> 01:48:00,562
So the detachment, the commanding officer,
and the officers of the Jews seized Jesus

1425
01:48:00,602 --> 01:48:07,382
and bound him, and led him to Annas first,
for he was father-in-law to Caiaphas, who

1426
01:48:07,422 --> 01:48:08,802
was high priest that year.

1427
01:48:09,262 --> 01:48:14,902
Now it was Caiaphas who advised the Jews
that it was expedient that one man should perish

1428
01:48:14,942 --> 01:48:15,842
for the people.

1429
01:48:16,762 --> 01:48:20,722
Simon Peter followed Jesus, as did another
disciple.

1430
01:48:21,642 --> 01:48:27,782
Now that disciple was known to the high
priest, and entered in with Jesus into the court

1431
01:48:27,822 --> 01:48:31,362
of the high priest; but Peter was standing
at the door outside.

1432
01:48:32,642 --> 01:48:38,282
So the other disciple, who was known to the
high priest, went out and spoke to her who

1433
01:48:38,322 --> 01:48:40,382
kept the door, and brought in Peter.

1434
01:48:41,502 --> 01:48:47,302
Then the maid who kept the door said to
Peter, “Are you also one of this man’s disciples?”

1435
01:48:48,122 --> 01:48:49,602
He said, “I am not.”

1436
01:48:50,022 --> 01:48:55,982
Now the servants and the officers were standing
there, having made a fire of coals, for

1437
01:48:56,022 --> 01:48:56,922
it was cold.

1438
01:48:57,602 --> 01:48:58,722
They were warming themselves.

1439
01:48:59,882 --> 01:49:03,182
Peter was with them, standing and warming
himself.

1440
01:49:04,262 --> 01:49:09,642
The high priest therefore asked Jesus
about his disciples and about his teaching.

1441
01:49:10,282 --> 01:49:14,022
Jesus answered him, “I spoke openly to the
world.

1442
01:49:14,762 --> 01:49:20,002
I always taught in synagogues and in the
temple, where the Jews always meet.

1443
01:49:21,062 --> 01:49:22,342
I said nothing in secret.

1444
01:49:23,282 --> 01:49:24,382
Why do you ask me?

1445
01:49:25,122 --> 01:49:27,862
Ask those who have heard me what I said to
them.

1446
01:49:28,562 --> 01:49:31,582
Behold, they know the things which I
said.”

1447
01:49:32,202 --> 01:49:39,262
When he had said this, one of the
officers standing by slapped Jesus with his hand, saying,

1448
01:49:39,822 --> 01:49:42,422
“Do you answer the high priest like that?”

1449
01:49:42,656 --> 01:49:49,396
Jesus answered him, “If I have spoken
evil, testify of the evil; but

1450
01:49:49,436 --> 01:49:51,556
if well, why do you beat me?”

1451
01:49:51,596 --> 01:49:56,076
Annas sent him bound to Caiaphas, the high
priest.

1452
01:49:56,696 --> 01:49:59,676
Now Simon Peter was standing and warming
himself.

1453
01:50:01,016 --> 01:50:06,276
They said therefore to him, “You aren’t
also one of his disciples, are you?”

1454
01:50:06,796 --> 01:50:09,396
He denied it and said, “I am not.”

1455
01:50:10,156 --> 01:50:16,116
One of the servants of the high priest, being
a relative of him whose ear Peter had cut

1456
01:50:16,156 --> 01:50:20,796
off, said, “Didn’t I see you in the garden
with him?”

1457
01:50:21,176 --> 01:50:25,776
Peter therefore denied it again, and
immediately the rooster crowed.

1458
01:50:26,256 --> 01:50:30,276
They led Jesus therefore from Caiaphas
into the Praetorium.

1459
01:50:30,316 --> 01:50:36,676
It was early, and they themselves didn’t
enter into the Praetorium, that they might not

1460
01:50:36,716 --> 01:50:39,796
be defiled, but might eat the Passover.

1461
01:50:40,976 --> 01:50:46,736
Pilate therefore went out to them and
said, “What accusation do you bring against this

1462
01:50:46,776 --> 01:50:47,676
man?”

1463
01:50:47,836 --> 01:50:53,836
They answered him, “If this man weren’t
an evildoer, we wouldn’t have delivered him up

1464
01:50:53,876 --> 01:50:54,776
to you.”

1465
01:50:55,156 --> 01:51:00,976
Pilate therefore said to them, “Take him
yourselves, and judge him according to your

1466
01:51:01,016 --> 01:51:01,916
law.”

1467
01:51:01,976 --> 01:51:08,256
Therefore the Jews said to him, “It is illegal
for us to put anyone to death,” that the

1468
01:51:08,296 --> 01:51:14,796
word of Jesus might be fulfilled, which he
spoke, signifying by what kind of death he

1469
01:51:14,836 --> 01:51:15,736
should die.

1470
01:51:16,036 --> 01:51:23,296
Pilate therefore entered again into the Praetorium,
called Jesus, and said to him, “Are

1471
01:51:23,336 --> 01:51:24,456
you the King of the Jews?”

1472
01:51:25,676 --> 01:51:31,896
Jesus answered him, “Do you say this by
yourself, or did others tell you about me?”

1473
01:51:31,936 --> 01:51:35,276
Pilate answered, “I’m not a Jew, am I?

1474
01:51:35,716 --> 01:51:39,156
Your own nation and the chief priests
delivered you to me.

1475
01:51:39,936 --> 01:51:40,836
What have you done?”

1476
01:51:41,736 --> 01:51:45,316
Jesus answered, “My Kingdom is not of this
world.

1477
01:51:46,216 --> 01:51:51,596
If my Kingdom were of this world, then
my servants would fight, that I wouldn’t be delivered

1478
01:51:51,636 --> 01:51:52,536
to the Jews.

1479
01:51:53,496 --> 01:51:55,776
But now my Kingdom is not from here.”

1480
01:51:56,436 --> 01:51:59,796
Pilate therefore said to him, “Are you a
king then?”

1481
01:52:00,716 --> 01:52:03,976
Jesus answered, “You say that I am a king.

1482
01:52:04,394 --> 01:52:10,274
For this reason I have been born, and for
this reason I have come into the world, that

1483
01:52:10,314 --> 01:52:11,914
I should testify to the truth.

1484
01:52:13,054 --> 01:52:16,554
Everyone who is of the truth listens to my
voice.”

1485
01:52:17,934 --> 01:52:20,254
Pilate said to him, “What is truth?”

1486
01:52:21,214 --> 01:52:27,654
When he had said this, he went out again to
the Jews, and said to them, “I find no basis

1487
01:52:27,694 --> 01:52:29,254
for a charge against him.

1488
01:52:29,794 --> 01:52:34,514
But you have a custom that I should
release someone to you at the Passover.

1489
01:52:35,734 --> 01:52:39,774
Therefore, do you want me to release to
you the King of the Jews?”

1490
01:52:40,614 --> 01:52:45,574
Then they all shouted again, saying, “Not
this man, but Barabbas!”

1491
01:52:46,374 --> 01:52:48,234
Now Barabbas was a robber.

1492
01:52:49,314 --> 01:52:51,434
John, chapter nineteen.

1493
01:52:51,474 --> 01:52:54,194
So Pilate then took Jesus and flogged him.

1494
01:52:54,994 --> 01:53:00,774
The soldiers twisted thorns into a crown and put
it on his head, and dressed him in a

1495
01:53:00,814 --> 01:53:01,714
purple garment.

1496
01:53:02,154 --> 01:53:04,694
They kept saying, “Hail, King of the
Jews!”

1497
01:53:05,374 --> 01:53:06,874
and they kept slapping him.

1498
01:53:08,054 --> 01:53:14,734
Then Pilate went out again, and said to
them, “Behold, I bring him out to you, that

